 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.\n- Bring the Required Tools & Material with you to the site\n\n**ARRIVAL:**\n\n- **CHECK IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER**–if you are unable to do so then you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.\n- **CHECK IN with Onsite POC / Manager: Introduce yourself as the QSIC Technician onsite for the Speaker Install Project, present the LOA and Verify Store Number**\n- **Call & Check-In with** the **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070**\n\n**ONSITE:**\n\n- REFER TO and FOLLOW Instructions called out in the Onsite Installation Guide - Any questions escalate to **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070**\n- **Ensure you clean up after yourself and dispose of any trash**\n\n**CLOSING OUT | COMPLETE BEFORE LEAVING SITE:**\n\n- Confirm device operation with Onsite POC\n- **Complete and Submit Online Deliverable** (Due back to Essintial PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE):\n- Tech will be asked to confirm site/location details\n- Tech will be asked to upload requested photos (Tech 1 / Lead Tech)\n- You will be asked to enter closing/completion notes\n- You will be asked to obtain Manager/POC Signature\n- Tech will be asked to provide the confirmation code received upon completion of your online deliverables.\n- **Call & Check-Out** with the **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070** to review/gain deliverable approval and perform your final check out\n- **Check-Out on your WO** - if you are unable to do so then you **MUST** call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in. **NOTE**: Your Check In and Check Out times must all match *(Work Order Platform and Final Check Out with Essintial)*\n\n**Closing / Completion Notes:**\n\n- Did you complete the online deliverable? If so, please provide confirmation code\n- Provide DETAILED notes of the work that took place including any problems and resolutions steps taken\n- Provide DETAILED notes of any problems onsite that would have caused a delay over 4 hours\n\n**ESCALATION:**\n\n- Support Related Questions and Any Issues onsite / Related to the scope of work should be escalated directly to the **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070**\n\n **Out of Scope Information:**\n\n- If you are asked to do anything onsite that is outside of the work scope on this work order or attached documents, please report to Essintial immediately for approval of additional/different scope.\n- If the instruction you are receiving onsite deviates from what is listed on your work order or attached documents, please report to Essintial immediately for approval of additional/different scope.\n- If the work onsite is about to go over the scoped/estimated time onsite, you MUST call Essintial immediately to provide the reason for going over that timeframe. You will also be required to provide this reason upon close out on your Online Deliverable.\n\n**PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS:** Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time.\n\n**DRESS CODE:** **Professional work dress code** is mandatory: Technicians should present a clean, professional appearance. A plain polo / collared / or button-down shirt, slacks / durable work pants (no shorts), and nice shoes / steel- or composite-toe slip-resistant shoes or boots. **Not allowed**: T‑shirts, hoodies, graphics, holes, or stained clothing.\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.\n- Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-15T08:00","end":"2026-10-15T12:00"},