{"job":{"id":20000218,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"P3 Global Services","title":"**HEXED** standee assembly - PLEASE, READ THE SERVICE DESCRIPTION COMPLETELY","description":{"html":"<p>IF YOU DO NOT AGREE WITH THE BELOW INFORMATION, DO NOT TAKE THE JOB.</p><p><strong><em><u>By accepting this work order you are agreeing to discount to $20 if you do not do the install for any reason out of your control. THIS INCLUDES IF A THEATRE HAS ALREADY ASSEMBLED PRIOR TO YOU ARRIVING, OR YOU CANNOT ASSEMBLE DUE TO DAMAGED OR MISSING PIECES.</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em><u>Any request for travel pay MUST be made as a counter-offer before job is accepted. Payment will only be made if you complete the job or if you are unable for any reason out of your control.</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em><u>Please do not call concerning schedule changes, missing pieces, etc. Only call if urgent, all other issues please send a message within Field Nation.&nbsp;ALMOST ALL ISSUES ARE NOT URGENT AND SHOULD BE SENT VIA MESSAGE.</u></em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>UNDER NO CIRCUMSTANCES ARE YOU TO REMOVE THE STANDEE FROM THEATRE PREMISES.</u></strong></p><p><strong><em><u>We cannot give you an estimate of the time it will take you to build this standee as everyone is different. You must review the attached instructions and estimate the time yourself.</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em><u>Please upload only ONE photo... either the completed standee or the manager's signature. Please do not upload ANY other photos.</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em><u>ANY delays beyond the stated schedule MUST be reported to P3 as soon as you know you will be late.</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em><u>Please, do not send counter offers via message. All counter offers must be sent using the counter offer option in Field Nation.</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><u> </u></strong></p><p><strong><u> </u></strong></p><p><strong>A standee is a free-standing, mostly or all cardboard display. Difficulty and time-involved can vary tremendously. Please review the public instructions before accepting.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>DO NOT INSTALL ANY OTHER ITEM WITHOUT FIRST GETTING APPROVAL FROM P3. IF YOU INSTALL AN ITEM OTHER THAN WHAT THE ORDER IS FOR, YOU WILL NOT BE PAID.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Tabs should never be visible while looking at the standee. If tabs are visible, you likely have made a mistake following the instructions</u>.</strong></p><p><strong><u>Overview</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em> WORK ORDER MUST BE CLOSED OUT&nbsp;<u>BEFORE 9AM EASTERN THE DAY AFTER THE DEADLINE</u>. Failure to do so could result in a 10% penalty or removal from the job.</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong> Note: Theatres will only allow installs Monday through Thursday. Do NOT attempt installs on Friday, Saturday, Sunday or holidays unless work order specifically notes it should be done or you have made arrangements with theatre management. Install can be done early if standee has delivered. <u>Do not go to the theatre if tracking has not been uploaded. Send a message to P3 via Field Nation messenger requesting tracking information.</u></strong></p><p><strong> </strong></p><p><strong>Package will be shipping directly to the theatre. Please check tracking at bottom of details tab before heading to the theatre.</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Looking for smart hand technicians to complete setup of Standee Displays</li><li>Standee&nbsp;for the motion picture “HEXED”&nbsp;</li><li>Please note that the only time requirement set forth by P3 is that the job be complete by the due date. Other than that, any specific dates/times are between you and the theatre and<strong>&nbsp;do not need communicated to P3</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>Please reach out to us via messages/email/phone only if there are issues or questions.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Pre-Site</u></strong></p><ol><li>Contact theater before leaving for site to verify that it is open. If you cannot reach site with the number in the work order, please Google the number or check Fandango.com for the first show time. Most theatres will open about 30 minutes prior to this first show. <strong><u>Do not ask if the standee has arrived. Use the tracking to determine this. Do NOT tell them you are calling to arrange a time to install a standee. You MUST go on site to attempt job to receive any payment.</u></strong></li><li>Read the service description completely. <strong><u>Review any instruction sheet that is attached to the order. If you feel that you cannot complete the instruction sheet at the agreed upon rate, let us know immediately.</u></strong></li><li>Set ETA.&nbsp;<strong>Please note, we will use this ETA to determine when the job will be done so please set it accurately. If you miss your ETA, we will begin questioning.</strong></li><li>Print out of the work order</li><li>Verify via tracking on details tab (note: this does not appear on Field Nation app) that package has arrived. <strong><u>If package has not arrived, DO NOT GO TO SITE. Send a message through Field Nation to P3 so we can research.</u></strong></li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Upon arrival:</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><ol><li>Check-in using the mobile app, unless there is a problem then contact P3 at&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(77, 77, 76);\">(661) 702-5153&nbsp;</span>&nbsp;if Monday-Friday between 9AM and 5:30PM PT. Otherwise, send message on Field Nation.&nbsp;Please only call if urgent. We have too many jobs to be taking superfluous&nbsp;calls. Most questions are answered below.</li><li>Ask for a manager to retrieve the package.</li><li>Find a location to start assembling the standee</li><li>Perform an inventory of the standee. If any missing or damaged pieces, place all pieces back in the shipping box and request theatre keep standee until replacement pieces are orders and installer can return. <strong><u>You must also note exactly which pieces (based on name or number on instruction sheet) are missing/ damaged in your closing notes</u>.</strong> Please do not order pieces yourself, this causes us to lose track of what has been ordered. <strong><u>DO NOT BEGIN ASSEMBLY UNTIL YOU HAVE CONFIRMED YOU HAVE ALL PARTS.</u></strong></li><li>Instructions and tools (if needed) are supplied in the box.&nbsp;<strong><u>DO NOT MODIFY THE STANDEE IN ANY WAY. STANDEE MUST BE ASSEMBLED EXACTLY AS PER INSTRUCTIONS.</u></strong></li><li>Take a photo from approx. 20 ft. away. The photo must clearly show the item in the theatre surroundings. If the install cannot happen for any reason, please try to get a copy of the work order signed by a manager and upload a photo of that. <strong><u>Please do not post \"work-in-progress\" photos. This will just slow you down. Also, under no circumstances should you upload photos of different items with the same title,, outside of theatre, items for different titles, etc.</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>Please upload only ONE photo of the COMPLETED standee unless advised otherwise, stand back while taking the picture so we are able to see the item in the theater setting (or, in case of denial, upload ONLY ONE photo of the work order signed by the manager on duty.&nbsp;If manager refuses to sign, upload a photo of \"REFUSED TO SIGN\" written on a piece of paper).</u></strong></li><li>Once completed with the install, place the standee in a high traffic area of the theatre’s choosing.</li><li>Get Manager on duty's name.</li><li>Make sure to close out the&nbsp;work order&nbsp;with notes.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong> </strong></p><p><strong><u> If Unable to Install for any reason noted below, follow instructions below (there is no reason to call about these issues):</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Note: You will not be paid if the denied install is due to your actions including arriving before item is delivered, arriving before theatre opens, standee is too complicated for you, arrived Friday through Sunday without approving it first with theatre, etc.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>If you can't install, follow these steps:&nbsp;</strong></p><ol><li><strong>If item is unable to be installed, request that theatre keep item for possible FedEx/ UPS pickup. If missing pieces, please note which specific pieces in closing notes and request theatre keep item for future install once replacement pieces arrive. UNDER NO CIRCUMSTANCES ARE YOU TO REMOVE THE STANDEE FROM THE THEATRE.</strong></li><li><strong>Check out of WO</strong></li><li><strong>Enter Close out notes of why you couldn't perform install</strong></li><li><strong>Take a picture of Manager Signature on WO as to Confirm they don't want the install to occur.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>Leave the item with the theatre manager.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>Enter a discount to bring payment down to $20. If this is not done, work order will be marked incomplete delaying payment.</strong></li></ol><p><br></p><p>Examples of denied install reasons:</p><ul><li>Already installed by theatre <strong><u>(in this case, we still need a photo of the installed standee. If not photo, no payment.)</u></strong></li><li>Not Playing Movie</li><li>Item Too Large</li><li>No Room to Accommodate at this Time -&nbsp;<strong>Please do not hold work order open if theatre does not have room at this time. Close it out and we will create another work order if our client request. You MUST also find out when they will have room. If not answered, the job will be kicked back.</strong></li><li>Requires Corporate Approval&nbsp;-&nbsp;<strong>Please do not hold work order open if theatre requires corporate approval. Close it out and we will create another work order if our client request.</strong></li><li>Content is Inappropriate</li><li>Theatre Requests Later Installation Date -&nbsp;<strong>Please do not hold work order open if theatre request later install. Close it out and we will create another work order if our client request.&nbsp;You MUST also find out what date they request we return. If not answered, the job will be kicked back.</strong></li><li>Theatre Does Not Display this Item</li><li>Theatre Unable to Locate Item -&nbsp;<strong>If tracking shows delivered, please close out work order. If tracking does not show delivered, please keep open and return once delivered. NEVER tell them that another will be sent. There is no guarantee that extras are available.</strong></li><li>Missing/Damaged Pieces -&nbsp;<strong>Please note the specific parts missing/damaged by the number in the instruction guide in your closing notes. Please do not order pieces yourself, this causes issues. Just note <u>EXACTLY BY NAME NOTED IN INSTRUCTIONS</u> which parts are missing in closing notes. </strong></li><li>Release Date Too Far Out -&nbsp;<strong>Please do not hold work order open if theatre request later install. Close it out and we will create another work order if our client request. You MUST also find out what date the theatre request that we return. If not answered, the job will be kicked back.</strong></li><li>Installed but not Functioning (please give further explanation)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>--- Very Important Additional Information ---</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>The agreed upon price covers all of your transportation expenses (fuel, taxi, Uber, tolls, etc), travel time, Field Nation fees and install time.</li><li>Verify via tracking on details/shipments tab (note: this does not appear on Field Nation app) that package has arrived.</li><li>Please review any attached instructions to confirm that you can complete the job in the allotted time and are comfortable with the agreed upon pay rate.</li><li>Please read the service description completely. This will answer 99% of the questions you may have.</li><li>If you go on-site before the theatre opens or before the item arrives, you will be asked to return without additional compensation.</li><li>Please adhere to the ETA that you enter. We monitor when jobs will be completed by this time.</li><li>Please note, we are only a fulfillment&nbsp;company and do not manufacture or design any of the items you will be installing. We will provide the manufacturer's instructions (when provided to us); but any questions about assembly will need to go to the manufacture (noted in the work order or on the instruction sheet).</li></ul>","markdown":"IF YOU DO NOT AGREE WITH THE BELOW INFORMATION, DO NOT TAKE THE JOB.\n\n***By accepting this work order you are agreeing to discount to $20 if you do not do the install for any reason out of your control. THIS INCLUDES IF A THEATRE HAS ALREADY ASSEMBLED PRIOR TO YOU ARRIVING, OR YOU CANNOT ASSEMBLE DUE TO DAMAGED OR MISSING PIECES.***\n\n***Any request for travel pay MUST be made as a counter-offer before job is accepted. Payment will only be made if you complete the job or if you are unable for any reason out of your control.***\n\n***Please do not call concerning schedule changes, missing pieces, etc. Only call if urgent, all other issues please send a message within Field Nation. ALMOST ALL ISSUES ARE NOT URGENT AND SHOULD BE SENT VIA MESSAGE.***\n\n**UNDER NO CIRCUMSTANCES ARE YOU TO REMOVE THE STANDEE FROM THEATRE PREMISES.**\n\n***We cannot give you an estimate of the time it will take you to build this standee as everyone is different. You must review the attached instructions and estimate the time yourself.***\n\n***Please upload only ONE photo... either the completed standee or the manager's signature. Please do not upload ANY other photos.***\n\n***ANY delays beyond the stated schedule MUST be reported to P3 as soon as you know you will be late.***\n\n***Please, do not send counter offers via message. All counter offers must be sent using the counter offer option in Field Nation.***\n\n**A standee is a free-standing, mostly or all cardboard display. Difficulty and time-involved can vary tremendously. Please review the public instructions before accepting.**\n\n**DO NOT INSTALL ANY OTHER ITEM WITHOUT FIRST GETTING APPROVAL FROM P3. IF YOU INSTALL AN ITEM OTHER THAN WHAT THE ORDER IS FOR, YOU WILL NOT BE PAID.**\n\n**Tabs should never be visible while looking at the standee. If tabs are visible, you likely have made a mistake following the instructions.**\n\n**Overview**\n\n ***WORK ORDER MUST BE CLOSED OUT BEFORE 9AM EASTERN THE DAY AFTER THE DEADLINE. Failure to do so could result in a 10% penalty or removal from the job.***\n\n **Note: Theatres will only allow installs Monday through Thursday. Do NOT attempt installs on Friday, Saturday, Sunday or holidays unless work order specifically notes it should be done or you have made arrangements with theatre management. Install can be done early if standee has delivered. Do not go to the theatre if tracking has not been uploaded. Send a message to P3 via Field Nation messenger requesting tracking information.**\n\n**Package will be shipping directly to the theatre. Please check tracking at bottom of details tab before heading to the theatre.**\n\n- Looking for smart hand technicians to complete setup of Standee Displays\n- Standee for the motion picture “HEXED”\n- Please note that the only time requirement set forth by P3 is that the job be complete by the due date. Other than that, any specific dates/times are between you and the theatre and **do not need communicated to P3**.\n- Please reach out to us via messages/email/phone only if there are issues or questions.\n\n**Pre-Site**\n\n1. Contact theater before leaving for site to verify that it is open. If you cannot reach site with the number in the work order, please Google the number or check Fandango.com for the first show time. Most theatres will open about 30 minutes prior to this first show. **Do not ask if the standee has arrived. Use the tracking to determine this. Do NOT tell them you are calling to arrange a time to install a standee. You MUST go on site to attempt job to receive any payment.**\n2. Read the service description completely. **Review any instruction sheet that is attached to the order. If you feel that you cannot complete the instruction sheet at the agreed upon rate, let us know immediately.**\n3. Set ETA. **Please note, we will use this ETA to determine when the job will be done so please set it accurately. If you miss your ETA, we will begin questioning.**\n4. Print out of the work order\n5. Verify via tracking on details tab (note: this does not appear on Field Nation app) that package has arrived. **If package has not arrived, DO NOT GO TO SITE. Send a message through Field Nation to P3 so we can research.**\n\n**Upon arrival:**\n\n1. Check-in using the mobile app, unless there is a problem then contact P3 at (661) 702-5153  if Monday-Friday between 9AM and 5:30PM PT. Otherwise, send message on Field Nation. Please only call if urgent. We have too many jobs to be taking superfluous calls. Most questions are answered below.\n2. Ask for a manager to retrieve the package.\n3. Find a location to start assembling the standee\n4. Perform an inventory of the standee. If any missing or damaged pieces, place all pieces back in the shipping box and request theatre keep standee until replacement pieces are orders and installer can return. **You must also note exactly which pieces (based on name or number on instruction sheet) are missing/ damaged in your closing notes.** Please do not order pieces yourself, this causes us to lose track of what has been ordered. **DO NOT BEGIN ASSEMBLY UNTIL YOU HAVE CONFIRMED YOU HAVE ALL PARTS.**\n5. Instructions and tools (if needed) are supplied in the box. **DO NOT MODIFY THE STANDEE IN ANY WAY. STANDEE MUST BE ASSEMBLED EXACTLY AS PER INSTRUCTIONS.**\n6. Take a photo from approx. 20 ft. away. The photo must clearly show the item in the theatre surroundings. If the install cannot happen for any reason, please try to get a copy of the work order signed by a manager and upload a photo of that. **Please do not post \"work-in-progress\" photos. This will just slow you down. Also, under no circumstances should you upload photos of different items with the same title,, outside of theatre, items for different titles, etc.**\n7. **Please upload only ONE photo of the COMPLETED standee unless advised otherwise, stand back while taking the picture so we are able to see the item in the theater setting (or, in case of denial, upload ONLY ONE photo of the work order signed by the manager on duty. If manager refuses to sign, upload a photo of \"REFUSED TO SIGN\" written on a piece of paper).**\n8. Once completed with the install, place the standee in a high traffic area of the theatre’s choosing.\n9. Get Manager on duty's name.\n10. Make sure to close out the work order with notes.\n\n **If Unable to Install for any reason noted below, follow instructions below (there is no reason to call about these issues):**\n\n**Note: You will not be paid if the denied install is due to your actions including arriving before item is delivered, arriving before theatre opens, standee is too complicated for you, arrived Friday through Sunday without approving it first with theatre, etc.**\n\n**If you can't install, follow these steps:**\n\n1. **If item is unable to be installed, request that theatre keep item for possible FedEx/ UPS pickup. If missing pieces, please note which specific pieces in closing notes and request theatre keep item for future install once replacement pieces arrive. UNDER NO CIRCUMSTANCES ARE YOU TO REMOVE THE STANDEE FROM THE THEATRE.**\n2. **Check out of WO**\n3. **Enter Close out notes of why you couldn't perform install**\n4. **Take a picture of Manager Signature on WO as to Confirm they don't want the install to occur.**\n5. **Leave the item with the theatre manager.**\n6. **Enter a discount to bring payment down to $20. If this is not done, work order will be marked incomplete delaying payment.**\n\nExamples of denied install reasons:\n\n- Already installed by theatre **(in this case, we still need a photo of the installed standee. If not photo, no payment.)**\n- Not Playing Movie\n- Item Too Large\n- No Room to Accommodate at this Time - **Please do not hold work order open if theatre does not have room at this time. Close it out and we will create another work order if our client request. You MUST also find out when they will have room. If not answered, the job will be kicked back.**\n- Requires Corporate Approval - **Please do not hold work order open if theatre requires corporate approval. Close it out and we will create another work order if our client request.**\n- Content is Inappropriate\n- Theatre Requests Later Installation Date - **Please do not hold work order open if theatre request later install. Close it out and we will create another work order if our client request. You MUST also find out what date they request we return. If not answered, the job will be kicked back.**\n- Theatre Does Not Display this Item\n- Theatre Unable to Locate Item - **If tracking shows delivered, please close out work order. If tracking does not show delivered, please keep open and return once delivered. NEVER tell them that another will be sent. There is no guarantee that extras are available.**\n- Missing/Damaged Pieces - **Please note the specific parts missing/damaged by the number in the instruction guide in your closing notes. Please do not order pieces yourself, this causes issues. Just note EXACTLY BY NAME NOTED IN INSTRUCTIONS which parts are missing in closing notes.**\n- Release Date Too Far Out - **Please do not hold work order open if theatre request later install. Close it out and we will create another work order if our client request. You MUST also find out what date the theatre request that we return. If not answered, the job will be kicked back.**\n- Installed but not Functioning (please give further explanation)\n\n**--- Very Important Additional Information ---**\n\n- The agreed upon price covers all of your transportation expenses (fuel, taxi, Uber, tolls, etc), travel time, Field Nation fees and install time.\n- Verify via tracking on details/shipments tab (note: this does not appear on Field Nation app) that package has arrived.\n- Please review any attached instructions to confirm that you can complete the job in the allotted time and are comfortable with the agreed upon pay rate.\n- Please read the service description completely. This will answer 99% of the questions you may have.\n- If you go on-site before the theatre opens or before the item arrives, you will be asked to return without additional compensation.\n- Please adhere to the ETA that you enter. We monitor when jobs will be completed by this time.\n- Please note, we are only a fulfillment company and do not manufacture or design any of the items you will be installing. We will provide the manufacturer's instructions (when provided to us); but any questions about assembly will need to go to the manufacture (noted in the work order or on the instruction sheet).","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00","end":"2026-09-24T22:00"},"payRange":{"min":125,"max":125},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":57},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/21/2026, 12:00:00 PM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-09-22T