{"job":{"id":20009575,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ASR tech","title":"Site Survey for Automated Locker System","description":{"html":"<p><strong>PLEASE READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING. YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ALL DELIVERABLES.</strong></p><p>Overview: This work order is to survey the location for a future install of an automated package holding locker in an apartment complex.</p><p>Background: Parcel Pending provides automated package(Fedex/UPS/USPS) holding lockers to apartment complexes. ASR is their onsite provider and installer.</p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><u>Indoor Zhilai - -</u></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><u>URGENT || Site Survey - Please request tech for a site walk ASAP before 9/28 due to delveiry booked - POC: Jacob @ 336-989-4226 - 8/31 - 7 indoor locker + 1 camera + 1 DS - site keep coming bak and says the area is according to FP - pleas ehave tech re measure the area and show to site about space issues - please send exp tech</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p><ul><li>Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.&nbsp;</li><li>Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.</li><li>Do not share any pricing information with client.&nbsp;</li><li>Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.</li><li>Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE</li><li>The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.</li></ul><p>ASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.</p><p>The Company explicitly prohibits:</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Main Contacts</u></strong></p><p><strong>Mark or Rodrigo (Phone numbers in confidential information)</strong></p><p>Please call on arrival and before you leave site. Also, please contact us if you have any issues or questions.</p><ul><li><strong><u>We have a FIRM start time with this order, you may arrive up to 15 minutes earlier.</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>For any delays or issues arriving on time, CALL Mark or Rodrigo.</u></strong></li></ul><p>Tech must include arrival and departure times, document any site delays, and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER</strong></p><p>========================</p><p>Project Number: 887</p><p>========================</p><p><strong>The accepting technician must meet ALL requirements below:</strong></p><p>Technician needs to know how to either mount a flat screen and/or install secure cabinet/fixtures to different types of walls(drywall w/ wood studs, drywall w/aluminum, plaster, Stucco, clay brick, cinder block or concrete.</p><p>Work order may NOT be rescheduled.&nbsp;Accepting tech is required to be on site the date listed, no exceptions.&nbsp;Tech is representing ASR and should refer to him/herself as an ASR technician when making contact with the MOD and calling into Parcel Pending. Tech should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with the Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR. If technician runs into DOA equipment/out of box failures, tech MUST contact ASR. Prior to going on site, please review the documentation and ASR sign off form (will be in the box)</p><p><br></p><p><strong>TOOL REQUIREMENT:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Government issued Identification</strong></li><li><strong>Standard Technicians tool kit</strong></li><li><strong>Standard 25' retractable tape measure minimum</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop with ethernet port to test for live internet.</strong></li><li><strong>AC outlet tester to test if power outlet is live.</strong></li><li><strong>Stud Finder</strong></li><li><strong>Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page</strong>&nbsp;(for checking in and out)</li><li><strong>Digital Camera</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Please bring PPE (Personal Protective Equipment). Not all sites require PPE but you will need to have it just in case.</strong></p><p><strong>PPE is hardhat, safety vest, safety goggles, long pants and steel toe boots.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Attachment:</strong></p><p>0887-SITESURVEYDOC-REV3-0.pdf&nbsp;- Print and bring to site.</p><p>=======================</p><p>READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER</p><p>DIRECTIONS</p><ol><li>Introduce yourself to the site contact as the ASR Techinician there to survey the Parcel Pending locker location</li><li>Follow the instructions that will be e-mailed to you to perform the site survey. Minimum items required are:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Sketch of room where lockers will be located outling doorways, windows, obstructions, data and power locations, any other items relevent to the locker placement.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Measurements of room where locker will be installed.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Measurements of walls, doorways, hallways that locker may need to pass through.</li></ul><ol><li>Take the photos outline in the instructions.</li><li>Have the manager sign off on the sign off sheet.</li><li>Upon completion, use the link provided in the e-mailed work order check out</li><li><strong>Upload all photos and survey to this work order and email them to parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com</strong></li><li><strong>Do not leave site until Mark, David, or Rodrigo have approved your work.</strong></li></ol><p>=======================</p><p>Site Aborts where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00</p><p>Site Abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site</p><p>Cancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.</p>","markdown":"**PLEASE READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING. YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ALL DELIVERABLES.**\n\nOverview: This work order is to survey the location for a future install of an automated package holding locker in an apartment complex.\n\nBackground: Parcel Pending provides automated package(Fedex/UPS/USPS) holding lockers to apartment complexes. ASR is their onsite provider and installer.\n\n**Indoor Zhilai - -**\n\n**URGENT || Site Survey - Please request tech for a site walk ASAP before 9/28 due to delveiry booked - POC: Jacob @ 336-989-4226 - 8/31 - 7 indoor locker + 1 camera + 1 DS - site keep coming bak and says the area is according to FP - pleas ehave tech re measure the area and show to site about space issues - please send exp tech**\n\n**ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS**\n\n- Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.\n- Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.\n- Do not share any pricing information with client.\n- Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.\n- Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE\n- The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.\n\nASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.\n\nThe Company explicitly prohibits:\n\n· The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.\n\n**Main Contacts**\n\n**Mark or Rodrigo (Phone numbers in confidential information)**\n\nPlease call on arrival and before you leave site. Also, please contact us if you have any issues or questions.\n\n- **We have a FIRM start time with this order, you may arrive up to 15 minutes earlier.**\n- **For any delays or issues arriving on time, CALL Mark or Rodrigo.**\n\nTech must include arrival and departure times, document any site delays, and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes.\n\n**READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER**\n\n========================\n\nProject Number: 887\n\n========================\n\n**The accepting technician must meet ALL requirements below:**\n\nTechnician needs to know how to either mount a flat screen and/or install secure cabinet/fixtures to different types of walls(drywall w/ wood studs, drywall w/aluminum, plaster, Stucco, clay brick, cinder block or concrete.\n\nWork order may NOT be rescheduled. Accepting tech is required to be on site the date listed, no exceptions. Tech is representing ASR and should refer to him/herself as an ASR technician when making contact with the MOD and calling into Parcel Pending. Tech should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with the Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR. If technician runs into DOA equipment/out of box failures, tech MUST contact ASR. Prior to going on site, please review the documentation and ASR sign off form (will be in the box)\n\n**TOOL REQUIREMENT:**\n\n- **Government issued Identification**\n- **Standard Technicians tool kit**\n- **Standard 25' retractable tape measure minimum**\n- **Laptop with ethernet port to test for live internet.**\n- **AC outlet tester to test if power outlet is live.**\n- **Stud Finder**\n- **Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page** (for checking in and out)\n- **Digital Camera**\n\n**Please bring PPE (Personal Protective Equipment). Not all sites require PPE but you will need to have it just in case.**\n\n**PPE is hardhat, safety vest, safety goggles, long pants and steel toe boots.**\n\n**Attachment:**\n\n0887-SITESURVEYDOC-REV3-0.pdf - Print and bring to site.\n\n=======================\n\nREAD THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER\n\nDIRECTIONS\n\n1. Introduce yourself to the site contact as the ASR Techinician there to survey the Parcel Pending locker location\n2. Follow the instructions that will be e-mailed to you to perform the site survey. Minimum items required are:\n\n- Sketch of room where lockers will be located outling doorways, windows, obstructions, data and power locations, any other items relevent to the locker placement.\n- Measurements of room where locker will be installed.\n- Measurements of walls, doorways, hallways that locker may need to pass through.\n\n1. Take the photos outline in the instructions.\n2. Have the manager sign off on the sign off sheet.\n3. Upon completion, use the link provided in the e-mailed work order check out\n4. **Upload all photos and survey to this work order and email them to parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com**\n5. **Do not leave site until Mark, David, or Rodrigo have approved your work.**\n\n=======================\n\nSite Aborts where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00\n\nSite Abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site\n\nCancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-23T10:00","end":"2026-09-23T11:00","latestStart":"2026-09-23T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":65},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":4},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $65 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790120612418}
{"job":{"id":20009526,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Unified Global Solutions","title":"Go Back for cutover at Xylem, Inc.","description":{"html":"<p><strong>VOIP / ATA Go-Back (Troubleshooting) – Technician Requirements</strong></p>\n<p>Unified Global Solutions is seeking a technician with Telecom and VoIP experience to resolve outstanding issues from a previous VOIP or VOIP-to-ATA installation.</p>\n<p><strong>Go-Back Scope / Anticipated Needs</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>SEND TECH FOR CUT OVER. DATE &amp; TIME COORDINATED WITH CUSTOMER IT.</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Any extra equipment left with the customer must be documented on the checklist (include what was left, who received it, and where it was placed).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Punctuality &amp; Assignment Rules</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Arrive on time. The customer is expecting you at the scheduled date/time.</li>\n<li>Late arrival may result in removal from this assignment and any bundled work orders.</li>\n<li>If another technician will complete the work, you must obtain Project Manager approval and provide their contact information.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Required Tools &amp; Supplies</p>\n<p><strong>You must bring all items listed below. Failure to arrive fully prepared may result in removal from the site and non-payment.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows laptop (Windows 10 or higher) with Gigabit RJ45 port</li>\n<li>Telephone butt set</li>\n<li>Cable toner and cable tester</li>\n<li>RJ45/RJ11 crimper</li>\n<li>110/66 punch-down tool</li>\n<li>Cable stripper and electrician scissors</li>\n<li>Telco banjo (or pair breakout tool)</li>\n<li>Multimeter</li>\n<li>Cable pulling rods and Fiche tape</li>\n<li>Drill, level, and stud finder</li>\n<li>6–8 ft ladder</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Supplies Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Minimum 500 ft of CAT5e cable</li>\n<li>6-pin RJ11 ends</li>\n<li>RJ45 jacks and keystone jacks</li>\n<li>Bridge clips</li>\n<li>Telephone splice connectors</li>\n<li>Patch cables and cable-making supplies</li>\n<li>Drywall screws/anchors and concrete screws</li>\n<li>Zip ties and Velcro wraps</li>\n<li>Wall plates and surface mount boxes</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> Bring any additional tools or supplies indicated during the site survey.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Dress Code</p>\n<p>Wear a clean, solid (non-logo) shirt with jeans or work pants.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Pre-Visit Instructions</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Read and understand all instructions and attached documentation.</li>\n<li>Confirm your ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Onsite Tasks</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check in on the Field Nation work order.</li>\n<li>Locate the onsite contact and introduce yourself as a Unified Global Solutions technician.</li>\n<li>Locate shipped parts and complete inventory.</li>\n<li>Inform support of any issues with the current system.</li>\n<li>Work with support to resolve outstanding issues and complete all tests.</li>\n<li>Clean up the work area.</li>\n<li>Remove old data/voice modem(s) if a new internet cutover is required.</li>\n<li>Give the onsite contact all removed equipment and any unused new equipment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Close-Out Tasks</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Have support verify completion with the onsite contact.</li>\n<li>Review the checklist with support. You will be released only after all tasks are verified.</li>\n<li>Upload all required deliverables to the Field Nation work order.</li>\n<li>Check out on the Field Nation app.</li>\n<li>The provider is responsible for all time increases and expenses added to the work order.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**VOIP / ATA Go-Back (Troubleshooting) – Technician Requirements**\n\nUnified Global Solutions is seeking a technician with Telecom and VoIP experience to resolve outstanding issues from a previous VOIP or VOIP-to-ATA installation.\n\n**Go-Back Scope / Anticipated Needs**\n\n***SEND TECH FOR CUT OVER. DATE & TIME COORDINATED WITH CUSTOMER IT.***\n\n**Additional Notes:**\n\n- Any extra equipment left with the customer must be documented on the checklist (include what was left, who received it, and where it was placed).\n\nPunctuality & Assignment Rules\n\n- Arrive on time. The customer is expecting you at the scheduled date/time.\n- Late arrival may result in removal from this assignment and any bundled work orders.\n- If another technician will complete the work, you must obtain Project Manager approval and provide their contact information.\n\nRequired Tools & Supplies\n\n**You must bring all items listed below. Failure to arrive fully prepared may result in removal from the site and non-payment.**\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Windows laptop (Windows 10 or higher) with Gigabit RJ45 port\n- Telephone butt set\n- Cable toner and cable tester\n- RJ45/RJ11 crimper\n- 110/66 punch-down tool\n- Cable stripper and electrician scissors\n- Telco banjo (or pair breakout tool)\n- Multimeter\n- Cable pulling rods and Fiche tape\n- Drill, level, and stud finder\n- 6–8 ft ladder\n\n**Supplies Required:**\n\n- Minimum 500 ft of CAT5e cable\n- 6-pin RJ11 ends\n- RJ45 jacks and keystone jacks\n- Bridge clips\n- Telephone splice connectors\n- Patch cables and cable-making supplies\n- Drywall screws/anchors and concrete screws\n- Zip ties and Velcro wraps\n- Wall plates and surface mount boxes\n\n**Note:** Bring any additional tools or supplies indicated during the site survey.\n\nDress Code\n\nWear a clean, solid (non-logo) shirt with jeans or work pants.\n\nPre-Visit Instructions\n\n- Read and understand all instructions and attached documentation.\n- Confirm your ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.\n\nOnsite Tasks\n\n- Check in on the Field Nation work order.\n- Locate the onsite contact and introduce yourself as a Unified Global Solutions technician.\n- Locate shipped parts and complete inventory.\n- Inform support of any issues with the current system.\n- Work with support to resolve outstanding issues and complete all tests.\n- Clean up the work area.\n- Remove old data/voice modem(s) if a new internet cutover is required.\n- Give the onsite contact all removed equipment and any unused new equipment.\n\nClose-Out Tasks\n\n- Have support verify completion with the onsite contact.\n- Review the checklist with support. You will be released only after all tasks are verified.\n- Upload all required deliverables to the Field Nation work order.\n- Check out on the Field Nation app.\n- The provider is responsible for all time increases and expenses added to the work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00","end":"2026-09-25T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":110},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":13},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $110 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso Durham"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.0