{"job":{"id":20011730,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Level 10","title":"Five Below | Install AP(s) Only | LIFT REQ","description":{"html":"<p>Overview</p><p>Level 10 tech will be onsite to perform an equipment upgrade to the access points. Check the location profile of each workorder for the specific access points that will be replaced. Not all access points will be upgraded, it varies by site. Work will start before store hours; it is imperative that all specified access points have been installed, tested, and the lift has been removed from site prior to store open. Tech must call into Level 10 Support to test and validate all access points are online. All the old equipment removed will get boxed up and placed in the Level 10 box that was shipped to site. Affix the return label that was sent in the box over the existing label for equipment to get shipped back to Level 10. Contact UPS to schedule a pickup, note the confirmation in CompanyCam checklist. Complete the CompanyCam checklist and have it reviewed and approved by Level 10 Support prior to leaving stie.</p><p>COMPANY CAM USAGE:</p><p>1. Go to this URL:https://app.companycam.com/projects</p><p>2. Enter any of these Usernames:</p><p>CompanyCam@Level10.com</p><p>CompanyCam2@Level10.com</p><p>CompanyCam3@Level10.com</p><p>3. Enter this Password: Level10!L10</p><p>4. Search for your Project by Site - Enter \"Customer and (site number)\"</p><p>5. Click on \"To Do's\"</p><p>6. Click on \"Checklists\"</p><p>7. Select appropriate checklist.</p><p>8. Upload all photos to the specified Checklist Only.</p><p>Tools Required</p><ul><li>Power &amp; Impact Drill 18v min.</li><li>Assorted drill, masonry, and driver bits</li><li>Fully charged Labeler w/white backed labels and black font</li><li>Fully charged phone w/Digital Camera and w/CompanyCam app installed</li><li>Velcro for cable management above the ceiling</li><li>Tie Wraps for cable management above the ceiling</li><li>Razor Knife</li><li>Sharpie/Permanent Marker</li><li>Cable Push/Pull Rods, fiberglass Fish Sticks, Glow Rods</li><li>Punch Down Tool w/66 &amp; 110 blades</li><li>Modular RJ45 Crimper</li><li>Data Tester</li><li>Toner w/Probe</li><li>Ladder 8ft min. (a multi-position ladder is recommended)</li><li>Flashlight</li><li>Electrician Scissors</li><li>Screwdriver Flatblade, Assorted</li><li>Screwdriver Phillips, Assorted</li><li>Allen Wrench Set</li><li>Torx Set w/Security</li><li>Level</li><li>Tape Measure 35ft</li><li>Pliers, Long Nose</li><li>Pliers, Lineman</li></ul><p><strong>Support Contact</strong></p><ul><li>Tech will need to contact (800) 807-1733 to check in/out and to report any issues.</li></ul><p><strong>Documentation</strong></p><ul><li>Five Below Refresh Network and Equipment - AP Only</li><li>Companycam checklist</li></ul><p><strong>Special Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Level 10 Technician will be required to work on a scissor lift in a new construction environment. Level 10 tech is responsible for providing all PPE as required by the General Contractor onsite.</li></ul><p>Deliverables</p><ul><li>Technician must have the CompanyCam app installed on their phone and have access to the site-specific CompanyCam project page. That page will contain a checklist that will need to be completed. This checklist will act as the required deliverables. Once the installation is complete, the checklist should have a green mark and a count (XX of XX) completed indicating that all deliverable items have been completed.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Expected Duration: 1.5 Hrs.</p>","markdown":"Overview\n\nLevel 10 tech will be onsite to perform an equipment upgrade to the access points. Check the location profile of each workorder for the specific access points that will be replaced. Not all access points will be upgraded, it varies by site. Work will start before store hours; it is imperative that all specified access points have been installed, tested, and the lift has been removed from site prior to store open. Tech must call into Level 10 Support to test and validate all access points are online. All the old equipment removed will get boxed up and placed in the Level 10 box that was shipped to site. Affix the return label that was sent in the box over the existing label for equipment to get shipped back to Level 10. Contact UPS to schedule a pickup, note the confirmation in CompanyCam checklist. Complete the CompanyCam checklist and have it reviewed and approved by Level 10 Support prior to leaving stie.\n\nCOMPANY CAM USAGE:\n\n1\\. Go to this URL:<https://app.companycam.com/projects>\n\n2\\. Enter any of these Usernames:\n\nCompanyCam@Level10.com\n\nCompanyCam2@Level10.com\n\nCompanyCam3@Level10.com\n\n3\\. Enter this Password: Level10!L10\n\n4\\. Search for your Project by Site - Enter \"Customer and (site number)\"\n\n5\\. Click on \"To Do's\"\n\n6\\. Click on \"Checklists\"\n\n7\\. Select appropriate checklist.\n\n8\\. Upload all photos to the specified Checklist Only.\n\nTools Required\n\n- Power & Impact Drill 18v min.\n- Assorted drill, masonry, and driver bits\n- Fully charged Labeler w/white backed labels and black font\n- Fully charged phone w/Digital Camera and w/CompanyCam app installed\n- Velcro for cable management above the ceiling\n- Tie Wraps for cable management above the ceiling\n- Razor Knife\n- Sharpie/Permanent Marker\n- Cable Push/Pull Rods, fiberglass Fish Sticks, Glow Rods\n- Punch Down Tool w/66 & 110 blades\n- Modular RJ45 Crimper\n- Data Tester\n- Toner w/Probe\n- Ladder 8ft min. (a multi-position ladder is recommended)\n- Flashlight\n- Electrician Scissors\n- Screwdriver Flatblade, Assorted\n- Screwdriver Phillips, Assorted\n- Allen Wrench Set\n- Torx Set w/Security\n- Level\n- Tape Measure 35ft\n- Pliers, Long Nose\n- Pliers, Lineman\n\n**Support Contact**\n\n- Tech will need to contact (800) 807-1733 to check in/out and to report any issues.\n\n**Documentation**\n\n- Five Below Refresh Network and Equipment - AP Only\n- Companycam checklist\n\n**Special Requirements**\n\n- Level 10 Technician will be required to work on a scissor lift in a new construction environment. Level 10 tech is responsible for providing all PPE as required by the General Contractor onsite.\n\nDeliverables\n\n- Technician must have the CompanyCam app installed on their phone and have access to the site-specific CompanyCam project page. That page will contain a checklist that will need to be completed. This checklist will act as the required deliverables. Once the installation is complete, the checklist should have a green mark and a count (XX of XX) completed indicating that all deliverable items have been completed.\n\nExpected Duration: 1.5 Hrs.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-30T08:00","end":"2026-09-30T09:30"},"payRange":{"min":125,"max":125},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":62},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $125 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM