{"job":{"id":"2729728300","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Level 10","title":"Public Storage | 3rd Party POS Installations","description":"<p><strong>Overview</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>L10 Tech will be onsite to complete a new store install by following the steps in the install guide. The L10 Tech will be picking up 4 to 6 large boxes (25x23x19) with the new equipment at a peer location which will require an oversized vehicle such as a van or pickup. All boxes will need to be transported safely to the new store location. If the tech is limited by size of car, additional trips back to the original location will be needed to pick up the equipment. Once the equipment is brought to the new location, the technician will follow the install steps as noted in the install guide.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Level 10 Tech is required to use the documentation listed below to complete this scope of work.</p><p><br></p><p>Cabling - A 2nd vendor is responsible for all cabling work -Tailwind, will be also onsite. They are responsible for the following as it relates to this installation:</p><ul><li>Tone, Test and Label all existing network drops where the new Public Storage PCs and printer will be installed.</li><li>Run new cat5e cables to any user station that needs network drops.</li><li>Each Public Storage User und workstation should have 3 labeled and tested network drops ran back to wherever the VMWare router, Cradle point and Netgear switch is located onsite.</li></ul><p><strong>Tools Required</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><ul><li><br></li><li>BATTERY DRILL WITH FULLY CHARGED BATTERY AND CHARGER</li><li><br></li><li>RAZOR KNIFE</li><li><br></li><li>SHARPIE OR EQUIVLANT PERM MARKER</li><li><br></li><li>8 LADDER</li><li><br></li><li>PUNCH ON TOOL WITH 66 &amp; 110 BLADES</li><li><br></li><li>DATA TESTER</li><li><br></li><li>CABLE CUTTERS</li><li><br></li><li>ASSORTED FLATBLADE SCREWDRIVERS</li><li><br></li><li>ASSORTED PHILLIPS SCREWDRIVERS</li><li><br></li><li>LEVEL</li><li><br></li><li>35' TAPE MEASURE</li><li><br></li><li>RJ-45 CRIMPER</li><li><br></li><li>FLASHLIGHT</li><li><br></li><li>SCISSORS</li><li><br></li><li>200 1/8\" STEEL FISH TAPE</li><li><br></li><li>ALLEN WRENCH SET</li><li><br></li><li>TELEPHONE BUTT SET</li><li><br></li><li>TONER W/ PROBE</li><li><br></li><li>DIGITAL CAMERA</li><li><br></li><li>P-TOUCH LABELER with LABELS</li><li><br></li><li>TYWRAPS FOR CABLE MANAGEMENT ABOVE CEILING</li><li><br></li><li>VELCRO FOR CABLE MANAGEMENT BELOW CEILING</li><li><br></li><li>WOOD SCREWS</li><li><br></li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Documentation</strong></p><ul><li>TEK_Public Storage 3rd Party Acquisition Guide</li><li>CompanyCam Checklist</li></ul><p><strong>Support</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Tech will need to contact the L10 Project Hotline at (800) 807-1733 to check in/out to report any issues.</li></ul><p><strong>Special Requirements</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><ul><li>L10 Technician will travel to a peer Public Storage address to pick up the equipment for the installation at the address of this work order:</li></ul><p>Deliverables</p><ul><li>Technician must have the CompanyCam app installed on their phone and have access to the site-specific CompanyCam project page. That page will contain a checklist that will need to be completed. This checklist will act as the required deliverables. Once the installation is complete, the checklist should have a green mark and a count (XX of XX) completed indicating that all deliverable items have been completed.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Expected Duration: 8 Hrs.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-07T10:00","end":"2026-10-07T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":429.42619118},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":24.7},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $429.42619118 is below minimum threshold