{"job":{"id":20012047,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Vimenture","title":"Phone/Network Setup Assessment","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Seeking a technician with experience in telecom/networking to assess and set up existing office phones at the new Foxwood leasing office.</li>\n<li>The leasing office is moving to <strong>6814 Fox Landing Way, Raleigh, NC 27616</strong>.</li>\n<li>The client will be moving the existing phones from the current office but will need assistance setting them up at the new location.</li>\n<li>The new office previously had Wi-Fi service and has existing Ethernet phone jacks.</li>\n<li>Technician will need to inspect the existing network infrastructure, Ethernet phone jacks, and available connectivity to determine what is required to get the phones operational.</li>\n<li>Job is estimated to take 1–2 hours.</li>\n<li>The technician assigned to this work order<strong>MUST</strong> be the technician performing the work on-site.</li>\n<li>The technician assigned to this work order<strong>MUST</strong> check in and out on-site using GPS, per our client's directive. If you cannot do this, please do not request this job.</li>\n<li>If any quotes are requested/required, these<strong>MUST</strong> be uploaded into Field Nation only and not shared with the site contact or our clients. Please include a breakdown of labor, materials, and any additional requested expenses.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Tools Required (<em>must haves</em>):</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop with Ethernet port or USB Ethernet adapter</li>\n<li>Ethernet/network cable tester</li>\n<li>Spare Ethernet patch cables</li>\n<li>Basic telecom/network troubleshooting tools</li>\n<li>Any tools needed to troubleshoot Ethernet phone jacks and phone connectivity</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>Pre-Site Requirements</em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Review the work order and call the work order manager with any questions before proceeding.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks</em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Check in to the work order using the Field Nation app.</li>\n<li>Introduce yourself to the onsite manager from Vimenture.</li>\n<li>Meet with the Community Director (CD) or onsite contact and confirm the locations for the existing phones.</li>\n<li>Inspect the existing Ethernet phone jacks and determine which jacks are active and properly connected.</li>\n<li>Inspect the available network/Internet equipment and determine how the phones should be connected at the new leasing office.</li>\n<li>Test Ethernet connectivity at the phone locations.</li>\n<li>Identify any missing, faulty, or required cabling, network equipment, configuration, or other items needed to complete the phone setup.</li>\n<li>Connect and configure the existing phones as applicable using the available infrastructure.</li>\n<li>Test the phones to confirm they have network connectivity and are operational.</li>\n<li>Confirm functionality with Property Staff.</li>\n<li>If additional work, materials, or equipment are required, document the requirements and provide a quote through Field Nation if requested.</li>\n<li>Collect a signature from the onsite manager.</li>\n<li>Clean the work area fully before leaving.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Required On-Site Deliverables:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Provide detailed notes documenting the existing network/phone infrastructure and what was required to get the phones operational.</li>\n<li>Document the results of testing each phone/jack worked on.</li>\n<li>Upload photos of the phone jacks, network equipment, and any relevant cabling/equipment.</li>\n<li>If additional work is required, clearly document what is needed and why.</li>\n<li>Check out of the work order in the Field Nation app.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Contact the work order manager if any of the following are true:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Clarification is needed on the work order or scope.</li>\n<li>The existing network/Internet service is not available or is not operational.</li>\n<li>Phone jacks are not connected or require new cabling.</li>\n<li>Additional equipment, materials, or labor are required beyond the approved scope.</li>\n<li>The technician is unable to complete the phone setup with the existing infrastructure.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Additional Hours and Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Buyer will not pay travel expenses unless pre-approved.</strong> Travel expenses must be entered in Counter Offers. Any pre-approved travel expenses must be entered in the Field Nation app as 'Travel Expenses' and not 'Additional Hours'.</li>\n<li>Any hours worked beyond the pre-approved maximum hours on the published job description must be pre-approved by calling the WO Manager. If approved, the buyer will document the additional approved time in the messages of the Field Nation portal.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in telecom/networking to assess and set up existing office phones at the new Foxwood leasing office.\n- The leasing office is moving to **6814 Fox Landing Way, Raleigh, NC 27616**.\n- The client will be moving the existing phones from the current office but will need assistance setting them up at the new location.\n- The new office previously had Wi-Fi service and has existing Ethernet phone jacks.\n- Technician will need to inspect the existing network infrastructure, Ethernet phone jacks, and available connectivity to determine what is required to get the phones operational.\n- Job is estimated to take 1–2 hours.\n- The technician assigned to this work order**MUST** be the technician performing the work on-site.\n- The technician assigned to this work order**MUST** check in and out on-site using GPS, per our client's directive. If you cannot do this, please do not request this job.\n- If any quotes are requested/required, these**MUST** be uploaded into Field Nation only and not shared with the site contact or our clients. Please include a breakdown of labor, materials, and any additional requested expenses.\n\n**Tools Required (*must haves*):**\n\n- Laptop with Ethernet port or USB Ethernet adapter\n- Ethernet/network cable tester\n- Spare Ethernet patch cables\n- Basic telecom/network troubleshooting tools\n- Any tools needed to troubleshoot Ethernet phone jacks and phone connectivity\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n***Pre-Site Requirements***\n\n1. Review the work order and call the work order manager with any questions before proceeding.\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n1. Check in to the work order using the Field Nation app.\n2. Introduce yourself to the onsite manager from Vimenture.\n3. Meet with the Community Director (CD) or onsite contact and confirm the locations for the existing phones.\n4. Inspect the existing Ethernet phone jacks and determine which jacks are active and properly connected.\n5. Inspect the available network/Internet equipment and determine how the phones should be connected at the new leasing office.\n6. Test Ethernet connectivity at the phone locations.\n7. Identify any missing, faulty, or required cabling, network equipment, configuration, or other items needed to complete the phone setup.\n8. Connect and configure the existing phones as applicable using the available infrastructure.\n9. Test the phones to confirm they have network connectivity and are operational.\n10. Confirm functionality with Property Staff.\n11. If additional work, materials, or equipment are required, document the requirements and provide a quote through Field Nation if requested.\n12. Collect a signature from the onsite manager.\n13. Clean the work area fully before leaving.\n\n**Required On-Site Deliverables:**\n\n1. Provide detailed notes documenting the existing network/phone infrastructure and what was required to get the phones operational.\n2. Document the results of testing each phone/jack worked on.\n3. Upload photos of the phone jacks, network equipment, and any relevant cabling/equipment.\n4. If additional work is required, clearly document what is needed and why.\n5. Check out of the work order in the Field Nation app.\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n**Contact the work order manager if any of the following are true:**\n\n- Clarification is needed on the work order or scope.\n- The existing network/Internet service is not available or is not operational.\n- Phone jacks are not connected or require new cabling.\n- Additional equipment, materials, or labor are required beyond the approved scope.\n- The technician is unable to complete the phone setup with the existing infrastructure.\n\n**Additional Hours and Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- **Buyer will not pay travel expenses unless pre-approved.** Travel expenses must be entered in Counter Offers. Any pre-approved travel expenses must be entered in the Field Nation app as 'Travel Expenses' and not 'Additional Hours'.\n- Any hours worked beyond the pre-approved maximum hours on the published job description must be pre-approved by calling the WO Manager. If approved, the buyer will document the additional approved time in the messages of the Field Nation portal.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-24T10:00","end":"2026-09-24T12:00","latestStart":"2026-09-24T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":10},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 (countered: $150) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":