{"job":{"id":20012617,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Tie National, LLC","title":"SonicWALL - Installation/Configuration Laptop, Patch Cables, Hot Spot Required","description":{"html":"<p>Contact Tie National, LLC (TIE) at 630-301-7444 Option #3, and then select option #1 to check in and check out of your service order #159490.</p><p><br></p><p>If you need any assistance or have any questions during your on-site service visit, please contact TIE's Technical Support - 630-301-7444 Option #3, and then select option #2.</p><p><br></p><p>Description of work requested:&nbsp;&nbsp;An onsite technician is required to install and configure a new SonicWall appliance.</p><p><br></p><p>The technician will be responsible for the following:</p><ul><li>Install and configure the new SonicWall firewall.</li><li>Verify the following network connections:</li><li><strong>X0</strong> – Cisco Switch</li><li><strong>X1</strong> – Cable Modem</li><li><strong>X2</strong> – Cellular Backup (if applicable)</li><li>Inspect and verify all network cabling and connections throughout the site.</li><li>Check the operational status of the cable modem, SonicWall, Cisco switch, and all related network equipment.</li><li>Test the internet connection and phone system to confirm all services are fully operational before leaving the site.</li><li>Coordinate with Tie National throughout the installation and troubleshooting process and provide status updates as needed.</li></ul><p><strong>Required Equipment:</strong></p><ul><li>Laptop</li><li>Mobile hotspot (for troubleshooting, if required)</li><li>Patch cables of varying lengths</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Gateway IP: 66.57.30.197</p><p>Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.252</p><p>First IP: 66.57.30.198</p><p>Last IP: 66.57.30.198</p><p>DNS1: 209.18.47.61</p><p>DNS2: 209.18.47.62</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>The technician must confirm that the firewall is configured correctly and that all network services are functioning properly before closing out the visit.</p><p><br></p><p>Tie National service order MUST be printed and brought to site on day of visit; before and after pictures of network area, server rack, cable management must be taken and uploaded to portal prior to leaving site.</p>","markdown":"Contact Tie National, LLC (TIE) at 630-301-7444 Option #3, and then select option #1 to check in and check out of your service order #159490.\n\nIf you need any assistance or have any questions during your on-site service visit, please contact TIE's Technical Support - 630-301-7444 Option #3, and then select option #2.\n\nDescription of work requested: An onsite technician is required to install and configure a new SonicWall appliance.\n\nThe technician will be responsible for the following:\n\n- Install and configure the new SonicWall firewall.\n- Verify the following network connections:\n- **X0** – Cisco Switch\n- **X1** – Cable Modem\n- **X2** – Cellular Backup (if applicable)\n- Inspect and verify all network cabling and connections throughout the site.\n- Check the operational status of the cable modem, SonicWall, Cisco switch, and all related network equipment.\n- Test the internet connection and phone system to confirm all services are fully operational before leaving the site.\n- Coordinate with Tie National throughout the installation and troubleshooting process and provide status updates as needed.\n\n**Required Equipment:**\n\n- Laptop\n- Mobile hotspot (for troubleshooting, if required)\n- Patch cables of varying lengths\n\nGateway IP: 66.57.30.197\n\nSubnet Mask: 255.255.255.252\n\nFirst IP: 66.57.30.198\n\nLast IP: 66.57.30.198\n\nDNS1: 209.18.47.61\n\nDNS2: 209.18.47.62\n\nThe technician must confirm that the firewall is configured correctly and that all network services are functioning properly before closing out the visit.\n\nTie National service order MUST be printed and brought to site on day of visit; before and after pictures of network area, server rack, cable management must be taken and uploaded to portal prior to leaving site.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-25T09:00","end":"2026-09-25T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":130},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":10},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $130 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","