{"job":{"id":20012681,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"DHD LP","title":"Mikrotik Router Install and TTU - Henry Schein, Raleigh, NC","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Statement of Work:</u></strong></p><p>Mikrotik router installation will take place at customer's site. When you arrive you will need to collect the router that has been shipped to the site and be escorted to the place of installation. Once technician is assigned,&nbsp;<del>*******</del> support team will send a Microsoft TEAMS bridge link for communication while on site.&nbsp;Technician will be shown to the circuit where router will be installed &amp; will provide access to our support team via Teams viewer or AnyDesk.&nbsp;Installation is considered completed once router is green lighted, confirmed configured, speed test is run and connection is confirmed. Windows Laptop Required,<strong>NO MAC</strong>.</p><p><strong><u>Field Tech Instructions:</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Prior to going onsite the following information is shared:</u></strong></p><ol><li><del>***</del> will introduce the Field Tech to the<del>*******</del> team including Email and Phone of the Field Tech</li><li><del>*******</del> Order Manager will send a Microsoft TEAMS invite directly to the Field Engineer for the time of install</li><li><del>*******</del> Support / Activation team will also provide the Supplier’s (Carrier) info directly to the Field Tech. This Carrier information includes looks something like the following:</li></ol><p>Make/Model::&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(56, 78, 115);\">RB4011IGS+RM</span></p><p>RG Serial: <span style=\"color: rgb(56, 78, 115);\">HMN0B3ZT6T1</span></p><p>MAC Address: XX-YY-ZZ-55-77-44</p><p>IP range : X to Y</p><p>Gateway : 108.XX.XXX.XX</p><p>Subnet: YYY.YYY.YYY.YYY</p><p><strong><u>Once onsite:</u></strong></p><p>- Troubleshooting capabilities are needed but<del>*******</del>/ End Customer is responsible for anything \"out of the ordinary\" (network / site issues, etc.)</p><ul><li>Technician must check in with the site contact upon arrival (contact info will be provided)</li><li>Technician must locate the circuit with the circuit ID or ISP-provided terminating modem/router.</li><li>Technician must connect CPE to the circuit and power on the device. After the equipment is on, technician should call us to test (bridge number will be provided, communication with customer will take place on Microsoft Teams call).</li><li>Technician connect Laptop to LAN port.</li><li>Laptop should be configured with public IP (to be confirmed by customer NOC)</li><li>Test Internet connectivity from laptop.</li><li>Please provide the screen capture of 3 Internet speed tests (Customer will walk you through this).</li><li>Please provide 3 photos of the router (label, router, rack).</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Field Tech Tool Kit:</u></strong></p><p>Technician needs to bring with them:</p><ul><li>Windows laptop (<strong>NO MAC</strong>) with Ethernet Port (<strong>GigaLAN</strong> – service max. speed: 200Mbps Bandwidth)</li><li>AnyDesk or TeamViewer installed on Laptop (<strong>NO MAC</strong>)</li><li>Basic hand tools to mount device</li><li>A mobile phone and a 3/4G internet card/similar device to access the internet and allow for remote access to the technician’s laptop.</li><li>The ability to disable Firewall and Antivirus software as it may be needed to get a clean speed test.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Statement of Work:**\n\nMikrotik router installation will take place at customer's site. When you arrive you will need to collect the router that has been shipped to the site and be escorted to the place of installation. Once technician is assigned, \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* support team will send a Microsoft TEAMS bridge link for communication while on site. Technician will be shown to the circuit where router will be installed & will provide access to our support team via Teams viewer or AnyDesk. Installation is considered completed once router is green lighted, confirmed configured, speed test is run and connection is confirmed. Windows Laptop Required,**NO MAC**.\n\n**Field Tech Instructions:**\n\n**Prior to going onsite the following information is shared:**\n\n1. \\*\\*\\* will introduce the Field Tech to the\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* team including Email and Phone of the Field Tech\n2. \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Order Manager will send a Microsoft TEAMS invite directly to the Field Engineer for the time of install\n3. \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Support / Activation team will also provide the Supplier’s (Carrier) info directly to the Field Tech. This Carrier information includes looks something like the following:\n\nMake/Model:: RB4011IGS+RM\n\nRG Serial: HMN0B3ZT6T1\n\nMAC Address: XX-YY-ZZ-55-77-44\n\nIP range : X to Y\n\nGateway : 108.XX.XXX.XX\n\nSubnet: YYY.YYY.YYY.YYY\n\n**Once onsite:**\n\n\\- Troubleshooting capabilities are needed but\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*/ End Customer is responsible for anything \"out of the ordinary\" (network / site issues, etc.)\n\n- Technician must check in with the site contact upon arrival (contact info will be provided)\n- Technician must locate the circuit with the circuit ID or ISP-provided terminating modem/router.\n- Technician must connect CPE to the circuit and power on the device. After the equipment is on, technician should call us to test (bridge number will be provided, communication with customer will take place on Microsoft Teams call).\n- Technician connect Laptop to LAN port.\n- Laptop should be configured with public IP (to be confirmed by customer NOC)\n- Test Internet connectivity from laptop.\n- Please provide the screen capture of 3 Internet speed tests (Customer will walk you through this).\n- Please provide 3 photos of the router (label, router, rack).\n\n**Field Tech Tool Kit:**\n\nTechnician needs to bring with them:\n\n- Windows laptop (**NO MAC**) with Ethernet Port (**GigaLAN** – service max. speed: 200Mbps Bandwidth)\n- AnyDesk or TeamViewer installed on Laptop (**NO MAC**)\n- Basic hand tools to mount device\n- A mobile phone and a 3/4G internet card/similar device to access the internet and allow for remote access to the technician’s laptop.\n- The ability to disable Firewall and Antivirus software as it may be needed to get a clean speed test.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-25T11:00","end":"2026-09-25T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":180},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":9},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $180 (countered: $180) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Foo