{"job":{"id":20012810,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"DataMax Service, Inc","title":"Install IT Hardware - Rack Mount UPS","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope Of Work:</u></strong></p><p>Once checked in, the technician should take the time to locate all inventory or devices to be worked on along with the areas we will need to access. The manager on duty, PM, and support will be able to help identify these if there is any confusion.&nbsp;</p><p>After the technician is ready to begin the SOW, the technician will need to work through the SOW outlined in the special notes field. If at any point you are confused on the SOW, refer to the attached documents for further support or reach out to the Project Manager.&nbsp;</p><p>Once the SOW has been completed, it is the technician’s responsibility to check that all devices, cable runs, and other equipment are all functioning and properly installed. Technicians must verify connectivity of all devices that we worked on prior to leaving site.&nbsp;</p><p>Each day that we are on site will require technicians to submit daily notes at the end of the day. We will also require a sign off sheet for each day we are on site. Technicians should send a message on this work order that outlines what was done on each days' visit and upload that days’ time sheet.</p><p><strong><u>Escalations</u></strong></p><p><strong>Problems on site - </strong>Datamax General Support Line <del>************</del></p><p><strong>Check in &amp; out - </strong>Customer Technical Support Line <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span></p><p><strong>SOW &amp; Tech Support - </strong>Customer Technical Support Line <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span></p><p><strong>Late or Cancellations - File a problem on your work order</strong></p><p><strong>Rescheduling or payment - File a problem on your work order</strong></p><p><strong><u>Check in and out Procedure</u></strong></p><p><strong>Check in</strong>&nbsp;with the following parties: Customer Support, and the platform.</p><p><strong>Check Out</strong>&nbsp;with the following parties: Customer Support, and the platform.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required tools: (Materials used will be reimbursed)</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>IF PARTS ON SITE ARE BROKEN OR MISSING CONTACT DATAMAX PROJECT MANAGER ASAP.</u></strong></p><ul><li>Cat5e (Plenum) or Cat6 Cabling</li><li>Data Wall Plates or Boxes</li><li>RJ-45 &amp; RJ-11 Network Connectors</li><li>Patch cables</li><li>Punch down tool</li><li>Cable Tester</li><li>Drill + Varying Bits</li><li>Wire Stripper</li><li>Laptop &amp; Smartphone with Wireless Hotspot</li><li>Labeling device</li><li>At least a 10' Ladder</li><li>Anything else needed to run a cable</li></ul><p>We have our company rates for equipment in the confidential information portion of this work order. These rates must be applied to materials that do not have a receipt.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Deliverables Required:</u></strong></p><p>1. Technician must check in and out with DataMax via the platform.</p><p>2. The technician must check-in and out with the Customer Help Desk via the help desk contact. ** Checkout will require a checkout code from the help desk**</p><p>3. Technicians must take pictures of any equipment requiring work done before any work is done.</p><p>4. The technician must work with the Customer Help Desk to complete the scope of work.</p><p>5. The technician must take pictures of any equipment worked on after the work is done.</p><p>6. The technician must report any customer requests made that are outside of the current scope of work to the Project Manager VIA Text, Phone, or Field Nation for approval.</p><p>7. The technician must post detailed closing notes including the name of who you worked with at Customer Support and any time spent waiting for the customer’s help desk or access to the site. If a Revisit is needed a detailed explanation as to why a revisit is needed and what will need to be done is required.</p><p><strong>** Failure to fulfill these requirements will result in a reduction of pay**</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Technician Requirements:&nbsp;&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p>1. Technician must be familiar with data cabling</p><p>2. Technician must be capable of running, testing, and terminating cable</p><p>3. Technician must be qualified to work on POS or Network Equipment</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Payment and Absence Policy:</u></strong></p><p>Payment for this work order is set at a predetermined rate. This fixed rate is meant to cover the entire dispatch.</p><p>If technicians are unable to make it to the site, the PM must be informed the day before. If there is an emergency, let the PM know ASAP.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Penalties and Bonuses:</u></strong></p><p>There will be penalties if technicians do not show up for a day that they are scheduled without informing the PM.&nbsp;</p><p>There are no eligible bonuses for this ticket.&nbsp;</p>","markdown":"**Scope Of Work:**\n\nOnce checked in, the technician should take the time to locate all inventory or devices to be worked on along with the areas we will need to access. The manager on duty, PM, and support will be able to help identify these if there is any confusion.\n\nAfter the technician is ready to begin the SOW, the technician will need to work through the SOW outlined in the special notes field. If at any point you are confused on the SOW, refer to the attached documents for further support or reach out to the Project Manager.\n\nOnce the SOW has been completed, it is the technician’s responsibility to check that all devices, cable runs, and other equipment are all functioning and properly installed. Technicians must verify connectivity of all devices that we worked on prior to leaving site.\n\nEach day that we are on site will require technicians to submit daily notes at the end of the day. We will also require a sign off sheet for each day we are on site. Technicians should send a message on this work order that outlines what was done on each days' visit and upload that days’ time sheet.\n\n**Escalations**\n\n**Problems on site -** Datamax General Support Line \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Check in & out -** Customer Technical Support Line \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**SOW & Tech Support -** Customer Technical Support Line \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Late or Cancellations - File a problem on your work order**\n\n**Rescheduling or payment - File a problem on your work order**\n\n**Check in and out Procedure**\n\n**Check in** with the following parties: Customer Support, and the platform.\n\n**Check Out** with the following parties: Customer Support, and the platform.\n\n**Required tools: (Materials used will be reimbursed)**\n\n**IF PARTS ON SITE ARE BROKEN OR MISSING CONTACT DATAMAX PROJECT MANAGER ASAP.**\n\n- Cat5e (Plenum) or Cat6 Cabling\n- Data Wall Plates or Boxes\n- RJ-45 & RJ-11 Network Connectors\n- Patch cables\n- Punch down tool\n- Cable Tester\n- Drill + Varying Bits\n- Wire Stripper\n- Laptop & Smartphone with Wireless Hotspot\n- Labeling device\n- At least a 10' Ladder\n- Anything else needed to run a cable\n\nWe have our company rates for equipment in the confidential information portion of this work order. These rates must be applied to materials that do not have a receipt.\n\n**Deliverables Required:**\n\n1\\. Technician must check in and out with DataMax via the platform.\n\n2\\. The technician must check-in and out with the Customer Help Desk via the help desk contact. \\*\\* Checkout will require a checkout code from the help desk\\*\\*\n\n3\\. Technicians must take pictures of any equipment requiring work done before any work is done.\n\n4\\. The technician must work with the Customer Help Desk to complete the scope of work.\n\n5\\. The technician must take pictures of any equipment worked on after the work is done.\n\n6\\. The technician must report any customer requests made that are outside of the current scope of work to the Project Manager VIA Text, Phone, or Field Nation for approval.\n\n7\\. The technician must post detailed closing notes including the name of who you worked with at Customer Support and any time spent waiting for the customer’s help desk or access to the site. If a Revisit is needed a detailed explanation as to why a revisit is needed and what will need to be done is required.\n\n**\\*\\* Failure to fulfill these requirements will result in a reduction of pay\\*\\***\n\n**Technician Requirements:**\n\n1\\. Technician must be familiar with data cabling\n\n2\\. Technician must be capable of running, testing, and terminating cable\n\n3\\. Technician must be qualified to work on POS or Network Equipment\n\n**Payment and Absence Policy:**\n\nPayment for this work order is set at a predetermined rate. This fixed rate is meant to cover the entire dispatch.\n\nIf technicians are unable to make it to the site, the PM must be informed the day before. If there is an emergency, let the PM know ASAP.\n\n**Penalties and Bonuses:**\n\nThere will be penalties if technicians do not show up for a day that they are scheduled without informing the PM.\n\nThere are no eligible bonuses for this ticket.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-30T06:30","end":"2026-09-30T07:30"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":175},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":65},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":55}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":8},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $175 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790179514055}
{"job":{"id":20008503,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Axiom Service Management LLC","title":"Diagnose and Repair - Zebra ZT620 - Printing too light -Troubleshoot only","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Work order description:</u></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Service manuals can be found at:</u>&nbsp;</strong>https://www.synergyitx.com/manuals</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Work Order Acceptance:</u></strong></p>\n<p>1. Do not bid on a Work Order unless you are qualified to work on the specified equipment.</p>\n<p>2. If awaiting dispatch instructions for a call, contact your dispatcher before proceeding to the onsite location.</p>\n<p>3. While onsite, providers are to exclusively represent themselves as HP technicians.</p>\n<p>4. Providers are authorized to work solely on the device specified in their Work Orders. Requests for additional work on other units should be directed to the customer's help desk.</p>\n<p>5. Providers must call dispatch after arriving onsite if experiencing any issues, including difficulties in locating the printer, finding parts, or the user.</p>\n<p>6. Exceptional customer service and communication are crucial for all service tickets. Providers are expected to adhere to general instructions. Failure to comply may result in delayed or non-payment.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Dress Code:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Providers are expected to adhere to a Business Casual dress code. This includes:</p>\n<p>- Slacks or Nice Jeans with no holes</p>\n<p>- Collared Shirt: Polo or Long Sleeve (Shirts with no logos or small logos are preferred)</p>\n<p>- Closed-toe Safety Shoes/Boots with protective Toe</p>\n<p>- Hard Hat and Vest</p>\n<p><strong><u>Required/Recommended Tools:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Providers should come prepared with the necessary tools for efficient service. These can include: Smart Phone, Vacuum, Alcohol, Q-tips, Wipes, Soft Bristle Brush, Canned Air, Light Machine Oil, Allen Wrenches (Metric and Standard), Digital Voltmeter, Assortment of Phillips and Flat Screwdrivers, and a Laptop and Wireless Hotspot.</p>\n<p><strong><u>NDA will need to be signed prior to work on site</u></strong></p>","markdown":"**Work order description:**\n\n**Service manuals can be found at:** <https://www.synergyitx.com/manuals>\n\n**Work Order Acceptance:**\n\n1\\. Do not bid on a Work Order unless you are qualified to work on the specified equipment.\n\n2\\. If awaiting dispatch instructions for a call, contact your dispatcher before proceeding to the onsite location.\n\n3\\. While onsite, providers are to exclusively represent themselves as HP technicians.\n\n4\\. Providers are authorized to work solely on the device specified in their Work Orders. Requests for additional work on other units should be directed to the customer's help desk.\n\n5\\. Providers must call dispatch after arriving onsite if experiencing any issues, including difficulties in locating the printer, finding parts, or the user.\n\n6\\. Exceptional customer service and communication are crucial for all service tickets. Providers are expected to adhere to general instructions. Failure to comply may result in delayed or non-payment.\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\nProviders are expected to adhere to a Business Casual dress code. This includes:\n\n\\- Slacks or Nice Jeans with no holes\n\n\\- Collared Shirt: Polo or Long Sleeve (Shirts with no logos or small logos are preferred)\n\n\\- Closed-toe Safety Shoes/Boots with protective Toe\n\n\\- Hard Hat and Vest\n\n**Required/Recommended Tools:**\n\nProviders should come prepared with the necessary tools for efficient service. These can include: Smart Phone, Vacuum, Alcohol, Q-tips, Wipes, Soft Bristle Brush, Canned Air, Light Machine Oil, Allen Wrenches (Metric and Standard), Digital Voltmeter, Assortment of Phillips and Flat Screwdrivers, and a Laptop and Wireless Hotspot.\n\n**NDA will need to be signed prior to work on site**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-23T08:00","end":"2026-09-23T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":33},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/23/2026, 8:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford,