{"job":{"id":20013419,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"REF#: 569566 - RALEIGH, NC - AV Rack & DirecTV Receiver (DTV RX) Service — Control, Cabling & Channel Change Diagnostics","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>It is required that the technician performing the on-site service is the same individual who was initially assigned to the job.</u></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of work:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Check-In &amp; Initial Inspection:</strong> Check in with site management, inspect the <del>**</del> rack, and ask if any additional display or control issues exist on-site.</li>\n<li><strong>Physical Connection Audit:</strong> Inspect all DirecTV Receiver (DTV RX) connections—including Power, Component, HDMI, Encoders, and AMX control lines—for loose, damaged, or broken cables. Ensure all power connections are securely seated.</li>\n<li><strong>Swap Receivers 6 &amp; 7:</strong> Physically and logically swap <strong>DTV 6</strong> and <strong>DTV 7</strong> to resolve the current control mapping mismatch.</li>\n<li><strong>Troubleshoot Rebooting Receivers (DTV 5 &amp; 8):</strong>Inspect power/signal supply on <strong>DTV 5</strong> and<strong>DTV 8</strong> to determine why they reboot when changing channels or opening menus.</li>\n<li><strong>Receiver Configuration &amp; CEC Verification:</strong>Verify every DTV box changes channels without rebooting, check that CEC settings are enabled, and ensure \"Allow Home\" is enabled in control settings.</li>\n<li><strong>End-to-End Signal Verification:</strong> Confirm clean video and audio signal flow from each DTV RX through encoders/matrix switchers out to the target monitors.</li>\n<li><strong>Document Replacement Needs:</strong> Clearly record serial numbers and model numbers for any faulty receivers or damaged cables needing full replacement.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Required Photo Deliverables</strong></p>\n<p><em>Upload the following mandatory photos under the</em><strong><em>Deliverables</em></strong> <em>tab upon task completion:</em></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Full AV Rack (Before &amp; After):</strong> Wide shot showing overall rack condition, cabling, and layout upon arrival and departure.</li>\n<li><strong>DTV 6 &amp; DTV 7 Swap:</strong> Photo clearly showing the updated physical placement and cabling for receivers 6 and 7.</li>\n<li><strong>Rebooting Units (DTV 5 &amp; 8):</strong> Close-up photos of the back panel connections and power supplies for DTV 5 and DTV 8.</li>\n<li><strong>AMX Control Connections:</strong> Clear photo showing control line wiring into the AMX system.</li>\n<li><strong>DTV On-Screen Control Settings:</strong> Photo of a monitor displaying the DTV menu showing <strong>CEC Enabled</strong> and <strong>Allow Home</strong> settings active.</li>\n<li><strong>Faulty Equipment / Model Serials:</strong> Close-up photos of serial/MAC stickers for any defective devices marked for replacement.</li>\n<li><strong>Signed Work Order:</strong> Photo of the physical sign-off sheet signed by site management upon checkout.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Complete all tasks listed in the WO.</li>\n<li>Represent the CLIENT professionally and keep the site clean. Dress code: Professional attire.</li>\n<li>Work closely with our remote support.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Date of Visit:</strong> 9/29/2026 at 9:00 AM(EDT)</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Tools &amp; Equipment Required</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Diagnostic &amp; Testing:</strong> Line Tester / Toner Probe (Audio Probe recommended), Windows Laptop with NIC port &amp; patch cable.</li>\n<li><strong>Hand &amp; Termination Tools:</strong> Basic Hand Tools, Cat5/Cat6 Termination Tools, Coax Termination Tools.</li>\n<li><strong>Lighting:</strong> Dedicated Flashlight or Headlamp (<strong>Phone flashlights are not permitted</strong>).</li>\n<li><strong>Consumables &amp; Hardware:</strong> Zip Ties, Velcro Straps, Electrical Tape, 16' Ladder.</li>\n<li><strong>Mobile Device:</strong> Fully charged Smartphone with camera for photo deliverables.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>1. Pre-Site Preparation</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Review:</strong>&nbsp;Study the WO and all attachments.</li>\n<li><strong>Inventory:</strong>&nbsp;Verify all shipped equipment and ensure you have all necessary tools/parts.</li>\n<li><strong>Support:</strong>&nbsp;Contact Support Tech with any pre-trip questions.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>2. On-Site Procedures</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Check-In:</strong>&nbsp;Log into the WO, call&nbsp;<strong>Support Tech (470-470-7757)</strong>, and introduce yourself to the On-site Contact/Manager.</li>\n<li><strong>Execution:</strong>&nbsp;Complete work, record the Manager on Duty’s name, and keep the work area clean.</li>\n<li><strong>Professionalism:</strong>&nbsp;Do&nbsp;<strong>not</strong>&nbsp;discuss Field Nation with the client; Support Tech handles all reporting.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>3. Required Deliverables</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Documentation:</strong>&nbsp;Detailed work notes and the Manager on Duty’s name.</li>\n<li><strong>Photos:</strong>&nbsp;Clear Before/During/After photos of the work.</li>\n<li><strong>Hardware:</strong>&nbsp;Serial and Model numbers (as applicable).</li>\n<li><strong>Completion:</strong>&nbsp;Confirm full functionality with remote support before check-out.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>4. Check-Out &amp; Submission</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Final Call:</strong>&nbsp;Contact&nbsp;<strong>Support Tech (470-470-7757)</strong>&nbsp;before leaving to review deliverables and obtain release code.</li>\n<li><strong>Deadline:</strong>&nbsp;Upload all deliverables and submit the WO within&nbsp;<strong>24 hours</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>⚠️Payment &amp; Expense Policy</strong></p>\n<p><strong>1. Flat Rate &amp; Travel Agreement</strong></p>\n<p>This is a <strong>fixed-budget assignment</strong>. By accepting this Work Order without a prior counteroffer, the Service Provider agrees the listed rate is <strong>all-inclusive</strong> of labor, tools, and travel.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Trip Charges:</strong> No \"Trip Charges,\" \"Fuel Surcharges,\" or \"Travel Fees\" will be approved if added after the work is completed.</li>\n<li><strong>Prior Approval:</strong> Any travel adjustments must have been submitted via counteroffer and approved by the Project/WO Manager <strong>prior to assignment</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>2. Onsite Hours &amp; Completion</strong></p>\n<p>All onsite hours will be compensated provided they are reasonable and the scope is fully completed.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Documentation:</strong> You must document any onsite delays or issues in the work order notes, clearly stating the reason for the delay.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>3. Unauthorized Expenses</strong></p>\n<p>Any expenses added to the final invoice that were not pre-authorized in writing via the platform's messaging system will be <strong>automatically rejected</strong>.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>⚠️ Compliance Alert</strong></p>\n<p>Reductions in pay or penalties may apply for:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Leaving site without posting deliverables or obtaining a release code.</li>\n<li>Failing to submit the WO within the 24-hour window.</li>\n<li><br /></li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**It is required that the technician performing the on-site service is the same individual who was initially assigned to the job.**\n\n**Scope of work:**\n\n1. **Check-In & Initial Inspection:** Check in with site management, inspect the \\*\\* rack, and ask if any additional display or control issues exist on-site.\n2. **Physical Connection Audit:** Inspect all DirecTV Receiver (DTV RX) connections—including Power, Component, HDMI, Encoders, and AMX control lines—for loose, damaged, or broken cables. Ensure all power connections are securely seated.\n3. **Swap Receivers 6 & 7:** Physically and logically swap **DTV 6** and **DTV 7** to resolve the current control mapping mismatch.\n4. **Troubleshoot Rebooting Receivers (DTV 5 & 8):**Inspect power/signal supply on **DTV 5** and**DTV 8** to determine why they reboot when changing channels or opening menus.\n5. **Receiver Configuration & CEC Verification:**Verify every DTV box changes channels without rebooting, check that CEC settings are enabled, and ensure \"Allow Home\" is enabled in control settings.\n6. **End-to-End Signal Verification:** Confirm clean video and audio signal flow from each DTV RX through encoders/matrix switchers out to the target monitors.\n7. **Document Replacement Needs:** Clearly record serial numbers and model numbers for any faulty receivers or damaged cables needing full replacement.\n\n**Required Photo Deliverables**\n\n*Upload the following mandatory photos under the****Deliverables*** *tab upon task completion:*\n\n1. **Full AV Rack (Before & After):** Wide shot showing overall rack condition, cabling, and layout upon arrival and departure.\n2. **DTV 6 & DTV 7 Swap:** Photo clearly showing the updated physical placement and cabling for receivers 6 and 7.\n3. **Rebooting Units (DTV 5 & 8):** Close-up photos of the back panel connections and power supplies for DTV 5 and DTV 8.\n4. **AMX Control Connections:** Clear photo showing control line wiring into the AMX system.\n5. **DTV On-Screen Control Settings:** Photo of a monitor displaying the DTV menu showing **CEC Enabled** and **Allow Home** settings active.\n6. **Faulty Equipment / Model Serials:** Close-up photos of serial/MAC stickers for any defective devices marked for replacement.\n7. **Signed Work Order:** Photo of the physical sign-off sheet signed by site management upon checkout.\n\n- Complete all tasks listed in the WO.\n- Represent the CLIENT professionally and keep the site clean. Dress code: Professional attire.\n- Work closely with our remote support.\n\n**Date of Visit:** 9/29/2026 at 9:00 AM(EDT)\n\n**Tools & Equipment Required**\n\n- **Diagnostic & Testing:** Line Tester / Toner Probe (Audio Probe recommended), Windows Laptop with NIC port & patch cable.\n- **Hand & Termination Tools:** Basic Hand Tools, Cat5/Cat6 Termination Tools, Coax Termination Tools.\n- **Lighting:** Dedicated Flashlight or Headlamp (**Phone flashlights are not permitted**).\n- **Consumables & Hardware:** Zip Ties, Velcro Straps, Electrical Tape, 16' Ladder.\n- **Mobile Device:** Fully charged Smartphone with camera for photo deliverables.\n\n**1. Pre-Site Preparation**\n\n- **Review:** Study the WO and all attachments.\n- **Inventory:** Verify all shipped equipment and ensure you have all necessary tools/parts.\n- **Support:** Contact Support Tech with any pre-trip questions.\n\n**2. On-Site Procedures**\n\n- **Check-In:** Log into the WO, call **Support Tech (470-470-7757)**, and introduce yourself to the On-site Contact/Manager.\n- **Execution:** Complete work, record the Manager on Duty’s name, and keep the work area clean.\n- **Professionalism:** Do **not** discuss Field Nation with the client; Support Tech handles all reporting.\n\n**3. Required Deliverables**\n\n- **Documentation:** Detailed work notes and the Manager on Duty’s name.\n- **Photos:** Clear Before/During/After photos of the work.\n- **Hardware:** Serial and Model numbers (as applicable).\n- **Completion:** Confirm full functionality with remote support before check-out.\n\n**4. Check-Out & Submission**\n\n- **Final Call:** Contact **Support Tech (470-470-7757)** before leaving to review deliverables and obtain release code.\n- **Deadline:** Upload all deliverables and submit the WO within **24 hours**.\n\n**⚠️Payment & Expense Policy**\n\n**1. Flat Rate & Travel Agreement**\n\nThis is a **fixed-budget assignment**. By accepting this Work Order without a prior counteroffer, the Service Provider agrees the listed rate is **all-inclusive** of labor, tools, and travel.\n\n- **Trip Charges:** No \"Trip Charges,\" \"Fuel Surcharges,\" or \"Travel Fees\" will be approved if added after the work is completed.\n- **Prior Approval:** Any travel adjustments must have been submitted via counteroffer and approved by the Project/WO Manager **prior to assignment**.\n\n**2. Onsite Hours & Completion**\n\nAll onsite hours will be compensated provided they are reasonable and the scope is fully completed.\n\n- **Documentation:** You must document any onsite delays or issues in the work order notes, clearly stating the reason for the delay.\n\n**3. Unauthorized Expenses**\n\nAny expenses added to the final invoice that were not pre-authorized in writing via the platform's messaging system will be **automatically rejected**.\n\n**⚠️ Compliance Alert**\n\nReductions in pay or penalties may apply for:\n\n- Leaving site without posting deliverables or obtaining a release code.\n- Failing to submit the WO within the 24-hour window.\n-","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-29T09:00","end":"2026-09-29T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":100},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":6},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790180984738}
{"job":{"id":20013476,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ASR tech","title":"Perform Maintenance on an Automated Package Locker System (MUST HAVE ALL REQUIRED TOOLS)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em>**PLEASE READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING*</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>*PLEASE READ PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK BEFORE ACCEPTING*</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>*PLEASE READ TOOL REQUIREMENT BEFORE ACCEPTING**</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>**PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK**</u></strong></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;The following has been reported:</em></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Indoor Zhilai - -</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">HIGH || Service Call - -Once onsite, Pls ONLY TEXT Josue at 949-427-1948. If no response within 5 mins, call Field Service team line 949-317-4169 </span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Parts sent out : 877522453061</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Requesting tech for 9/24 after 1130am, EDT </span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Need to: replace lock on center panel. might need to drill out old lock with key stuck inside</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">PLS ROUTE TO AN EXPERIENCED TECH pls have tech take laptop, usb keyboard, patch cable, hotspot if available and tools to check locker connections pls route to a experienced tech </span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- General Maintenance (Open All Box, Package Maintenance, Disabled Doors, Test Camera, Barcode scanner) </span></p><p><em>ensure the system is fully functional. General Linux, electrical, and mechanical knowledge is required, but technical support will guide you through most of the process.</em><strong><em>Professionalism and attention to detail are required for this client.&nbsp;&nbsp;Please be mindful of how you are representing ASR and yourself.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>**TOOL REQUIREMENT**ALL TOOLS LISTED ARE REQUIRED**</u></strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><strong>Government issued Identification</strong></li><li><strong>Standard Technicians tool kit</strong></li><li><strong>Precision screwdriver set</strong></li><li><strong>Rubber Mallet</strong></li><li><strong>4' ladder</strong></li><li><strong>5\" round reusable hard surface sliders (or similar for floor protection)</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop w/ HyperTerminal or Putty, must be able to connect to CAT5 Cable and runs Windows XP or higher</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop must have Team Viewer</strong></li><li><strong>Drill/Driver</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop Charger</strong></li><li><strong>Wired USB Keyboard</strong></li><li><strong>6ft Crossover patch cable</strong></li><li><strong>6ft Standard patch cable</strong></li><li><strong>22-16 AWG&nbsp;wire splicing connectors</strong></li><li><strong>Silicone caulking (for end of self-tapping screws)</strong></li><li><strong>Crimper/Stripper tool</strong></li><li><strong>Punch Down tool (used to terminate keystone jacks)</strong></li><li><strong>Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page, Camera, Text</strong></li><li><strong>Smart Phone Charger</strong></li><li><strong>Digital Camera or the Smart Phone Camera (Must upload all photos of equipment worked on)</strong></li><li><strong>Dry Cloth/Towel and non-abrasive cleaner (wipe down lockers before leaving site)</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Download, print, review, and bring the attached PDFs to site:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>ServiceCallChecklist rev1_1.pdf</li><li>0887-SYSTEMMAINTENANCEDOC-REV2-2a.pdf</li></ul><p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK MAY include open all box test, redelivering all packages, check for jammed/disabled doors, etc.</strong></p><p><strong>Some issues may take longer than expected.&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Potential issues can include any or all of the following:</p><ul><li>Jammed Door</li><li>Controller Unit Replacement</li><li>Sub Board Replacement</li><li>Solenoid Replacement</li><li>Clear Box/Redeliver Packages</li><li>If parts are to be returned, please use the prepaid return label provided</li><li>IMPORTANT:Please Take Photos of the equipment and parts before packing and returning</li></ul><p><strong><em><u>Professionalism, attention to detail, and customer care are required for this client, Customer Service skills are a must!&nbsp;Any discussion of prior work performed by anyone is not allowed. This may be reported back to Parcel and ASR. It may be interpreted as unprofessional behavior.</u></em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>iTEK PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Technician should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR.</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>If the customer reaches out directly to you, please refer them back to ASR.</u></strong></p><ul><li>Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.&nbsp;</li><li>Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.</li><li>Do not share any pricing information with client.&nbsp;</li><li>Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.</li><li>Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE</li><li>The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>The Company explicitly prohibits:</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.</u></strong></p><p><strong><em><u>ASR Project Number: 887</u></em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Client requires TIMELY arrival. Please make every effort to arrive on time to avoid penalty.</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Parcel Pending provides automated package (Fedex/UPS/USPS) holding lockers to apartment complexes. ASR is their onsite provider and installer.</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>STEP ONE:</u></strong></p><p><strong>CHECK-IN: With Parcel Pending, be mindful as you are in contact with the customer directly (your contact name and number is listed under the Problem Description)&nbsp;Ask if any Parts were shipped to site and who has the parts onsite. DO NOT PERFORM ANY WORK&nbsp;until you have contacted Parcel Pending.&nbsp;&nbsp;Please only contact our customer when you have arrived onsite and ready to perform work.</strong></p><p><strong>***Always Leave a message if your contact does not answer and then call their Field Service line&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span>***</p><p><strong><u>STEP TWO:</u></strong></p><p><strong>CHECK-IN: On Field Nation - Please do not check in on&nbsp;Field Nation until you have checked in with Parcel Pending.&nbsp;​Your check-in/out times MUST match what Parcel Pending provides us.</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP THREE:</u></strong></p><p><strong>LOCATE: Leasing/Rental Office, General Contractors Office, Concierge, Front Desk etc. Once in contact, ask for parts, if they were shipped.&nbsp;You would have this information from your contact in step one.</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP FOUR:</u></strong></p><p><strong>FOLLOW: Direction from Parcel Pending.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP FIVE:</u></strong></p><p><strong>REPORT: PROBLEMS/ISSUES&nbsp;BEFORE LEAVING SITE and&nbsp;<u>CHECK-OUT.</u>&nbsp;&nbsp;Please do NOT check out on Field Nation until you have checked out with Parcel Pending.&nbsp;​(Number and tech support name will be under the Problem Description</strong>)&nbsp;<strong>Your check-in/out times MUST match what our customer provides us.</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP SIX:</u></strong></p><p><strong>SUBMIT</strong>: W<strong>ork order for payment within 24 hours of scheduled date.&nbsp;</strong>Please provide&nbsp;<strong>detailed closing notes</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>timeline&nbsp;</strong>when submitting this work order for payment.</p><p><strong><em>The name of the individual accepting this work must be the actual person who arrives on site and if we determine there was a substitution without prior notice, we will not pay for the work performed.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Be sure to notify ASR by phone and message in work order prior to tech arriving onsite.&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong>ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER MEANS THAT YOU WILL HAVE ALL OF THE REQUIRED TOOLS.&nbsp;ALSO, HAVE READ AND UNDERSTAND THE SCOPE OF WORK.&nbsp;&nbsp;PLEASE UPDATE YOUR ETA AS SOON AS YOU ARE ASSIGNED.&nbsp;YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ARRIVING ON THE SCHEDULED DATE AND TIME. ANY VIOLATIONS WILL BE ESCALATED TO FIELD NATION.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><em>Parcel Pending and Site may provide a report card based on professionalism and understanding of work being done.&nbsp;</em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Tech should NOT discuss payment or scheduling discrepancies with Parcel Pending, Site Contact or anyone but ASR (NO exceptions)</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>***Please CALL Rodrigo R.</strong> <strong>949-556-3604</strong>&nbsp;for any general questions/information.***</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ONSITE DETAILS &amp; CONDUCT</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>If you are unable to make it to site, you must call/text Rodrigo.</strong>&nbsp;(Phone number in Confidential Information)</li><li><strong>Work Order is subject to Penalty Fee at Buyers Discretion.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>You will be representing ASR Services when communicating with the end user or Parcel Pending support.</strong></li><li><strong>All conversation on site should be kept to business related items and not personal matters.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>Resolve the issues using the documentation provided with support from Technical Support.</strong></li><li><strong>Do not access the \"System Maintenance Screen\" unless instructed by Technical Support.</strong></li><li><strong><u>Upon completion of service:&nbsp;KEY NEEDS TO BE IN SECURE LOCATION</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>a: please return keys to MOD onsite. Will need first and last name of keyholder (this info is required for release from site and Work Order closure).</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>b: If no onsite personnel are onsite/available, ask Parcel Pending Support/ASR Support Team member with whom you are working for direction on where keys should be left.&nbsp;</u></strong></li><li><strong>If you are requested to do anything out side of the scope of work, including returning to site, or dealing with a DOA, you must call/text Rodrigo.&nbsp;</strong>(Phone number in Confidential Information)</li><li><strong>Tech must provide photos of any equipment that is worked on.</strong></li><li><strong>Tech must fill out the ServiceCallChecklist rev1_1.pdf COMPLETELY and have it signed by the property manager</strong></li><li><strong>Tech must note arrival and departure times on sign off sheet, document any site delays and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes.</strong></li><li><strong>During completion, tech must provide any photos, closing notes, open issues, service call checklist, sign off sheet, and name of person that released tech from site.</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>RETURNING EQUIPMENT</u></strong></p><p><strong>If any equipment needs to be returned to Parcel Pending after completion please take a photo of equipment or parts before leaving site (damaged or undamaged) to ensure responsibility.&nbsp;A return label will be in the shipping pouch behind the original shipping label.</strong></p><p><strong>If a return label was not provided, please contact Parcel Pending immediately to obtain BEFORE leaving site, they will email a return label to you.</strong></p><p><strong>***A release code will be provided to you once tracking shows that parts are on the way back to our customer***</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>PAYMENT</u></strong></p><p>2 hours on site will be paid at a fixed rate of $85 with a potential of up to 2 additional hours paid in 15 min intervals @ $40/hr.</p><p><strong>Some issues may take long.&nbsp;Any time on site, after 2 hours, will need to be approved by Parcel Pending.</strong></p><p><strong>Your check in/out times on this work order must match what our customer provides.</strong></p><p>Site abort where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00</p><p>Site abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site.</p><p>Cancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.</p>","markdown":"***\\*\\*PLEASE READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING\\****\n\n***\\*PLEASE READ PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK BEFORE ACCEPTING\\****\n\n***\\*PLEASE READ TOOL REQUIREMENT BEFORE ACCEPTING\\*\\****\n\n**\\*\\*PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK\\*\\***\n\n ***The following has been reported:***\n\nIndoor Zhilai - -\n\nHIGH || Service Call - -Once onsite, Pls ONLY TEXT Josue at 949-427-1948. If no response within 5 mins, call Field Service team line 949-317-4169\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\- Parts sent out : 877522453061\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\- Requesting tech for 9/24 after 1130am, EDT\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\- Need to: replace lock on center panel. might need to drill out old lock with key stuck inside\n\nPLS ROUTE TO AN EXPERIENCED TECH pls have tech take laptop, usb keyboard, patch cable, hotspot if available and tools to check locker connections pls route to a experienced tech\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\- General Maintenance (Open All Box, Package Maintenance, Disabled Doors, Test Camera, Barcode scanner)\n\n*ensure the system is fully functional. General Linux, electrical, and mechanical knowledge is required, but technical support will guide you through most of the process.****Professionalism and attention to detail are required for this client. Please be mindful of how you are representing ASR and yourself.***\n\n**\\*\\*TOOL REQUIREMENT\\*\\*ALL TOOLS LISTED ARE REQUIRED\\*\\***\n\n- **Government issued Identification**\n- **Standard Technicians tool kit**\n- **Precision screwdriver set**\n- **Rubber Mallet**\n- **4' ladder**\n- **5\" round reusable hard surface sliders (or similar for floor protection)**\n- **Laptop w/ HyperTerminal or Putty, must be able to connect to CAT5 Cable and runs Windows XP or higher**\n- **Laptop must have Team Viewer**\n- **Drill/Driver**\n- **Laptop Charger**\n- **Wired USB Keyboard**\n- **6ft Crossover patch cable**\n- **6ft Standard patch cable**\n- **22-16 AWG wire splicing connectors**\n- **Silicone caulking (for end of self-tapping screws)**\n- **Crimper/Stripper tool**\n- **Punch Down tool (used to terminate keystone jacks)**\n- **Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page, Camera, Text**\n- **Smart Phone Charger**\n- **Digital Camera or the Smart Phone Camera (Must upload all photos of equipment worked on)**\n- **Dry Cloth/Towel and non-abrasive cleaner (wipe down lockers before leaving site)**\n\n**Download, print, review, and bring the attached PDFs to site:**\n\n- ServiceCallChecklist rev1\\_1.pdf\n- 0887-SYSTEMMAINTENANCEDOC-REV2-2a.pdf\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK MAY include open all box test, redelivering all packages, check for jammed/disabled doors, etc.**\n\n**Some issues may take longer than expected.**\n\nPotential issues can include any or all of the following:\n\n- Jammed Door\n- Controller Unit Replacement\n- Sub Board Replacement\n- Solenoid Replacement\n- Clear Box/Redeliver Packages\n- If parts are to be returned, please use the prepaid return label provided\n- IMPORTANT:Please Take Photos of the equipment and parts before packing and returning\n\n***Professionalism, attention to detail, and customer care are required for this client, Customer Service skills are a must! Any discussion of prior work performed by anyone is not allowed. This may be reported back to Parcel and ASR. It may be interpreted as unprofessional behavior.***\n\n**iTEK PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS**\n\n**Technician should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR.**\n\n**If the customer reaches out directly to you, please refer them back to ASR.**\n\n- Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.\n- Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.\n- Do not share any pricing information with client.\n- Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.\n- Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE\n- The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.\n\n**ASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.**\n\n**The Company explicitly prohibits:**\n\n**The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.**\n\n***ASR Project Number: 887***\n\n***Client requires TIMELY arrival. Please make every effort to arrive on time to avoid penalty.***\n\n***Parcel Pending provides automated package (Fedex/UPS/USPS) holding lockers to apartment complexes. ASR is their onsite provider and installer.***\n\n**STEP ONE:**\n\n**CHECK-IN: With Parcel Pending, be mindful as you are in contact with the customer directly (your contact name and number is listed under the Problem Description) Ask if any Parts were shipped to site and who has the parts onsite. DO NOT PERFORM ANY WORK until you have contacted Parcel Pending. Please only contact our customer when you have arrived onsite and ready to perform work.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Always Leave a message if your contact does not answer and then call their Field Service line** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**STEP TWO:**\n\n**CHECK-IN: On Field Nation - Please do not check in on Field Nation until you have checked in with Parcel Pending. ​Your check-in/out times MUST match what Parcel Pending provides us.**\n\n**STEP THREE:**\n\n**LOCATE: Leasing/Rental Office, General Contractors Office, Concierge, Front Desk etc. Once in contact, ask for parts, if they were shipped. You would have this information from your contact in step one.**\n\n**STEP FOUR:**\n\n**FOLLOW: Direction from Parcel Pending.**\n\n**STEP FIVE:**\n\n**REPORT: PROBLEMS/ISSUES BEFORE LEAVING SITE and CHECK-OUT. Please do NOT check out on Field Nation until you have checked out with Parcel Pending. ​(Number and tech support name will be under the Problem Description**) **Your check-in/out times MUST match what our customer provides us.**\n\n**STEP SIX:**\n\n**SUBMIT**: W**ork order for payment within 24 hours of scheduled date.** Please provide **detailed closing notes** and **timeline** when submitting this work order for payment.\n\n***The name of the individual accepting this work must be the actual person who arrives on site and if we determine there was a substitution without prior notice, we will not pay for the work performed.***\n\n***Be sure to notify ASR by phone and message in work order prior to tech arriving onsite.***\n\n**ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER MEANS THAT YOU WILL HAVE ALL OF THE REQUIRED TOOLS. ALSO, HAVE READ AND UNDERSTAND THE SCOPE OF WORK. PLEASE UPDATE YOUR ETA AS SOON AS YOU ARE ASSIGNED. YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ARRIVING ON THE SCHEDULED DATE AND TIME. ANY VIOLATIONS WILL BE ESCALATED TO FIELD NATION.**\n\n***Parcel Pending and Site may provide a report card based on professionalism and understanding of work being done.***\n\n**Tech should NOT discuss payment or scheduling discrepancies with Parcel Pending, Site Contact or anyone but ASR (NO exceptions)**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Please CALL Rodrigo R.** **949-556-3604** for any general questions/information.\\*\\*\\*\n\n**ONSITE DETAILS & CONDUCT**\n\n- **If you are unable to make it to site, you must call/text Rodrigo.** (Phone number in Confidential Information)\n- **Work Order is subject to Penalty Fee at Buyers Discretion.**\n- **You will be representing ASR Services when communicating with the end user or Parcel Pending support.**\n- **All conversation on site should be kept to business related items and not personal matters.**\n- **Resolve the issues using the documentation provided with support from Technical Support.**\n- **Do not access the \"System Maintenance Screen\" unless instructed by Technical Support.**\n- **Upon completion of service: KEY NEEDS TO BE IN SECURE LOCATION**\n- **a: please return keys to MOD onsite. Will need first and last name of keyholder (this info is required for release from site and Work Order closure).**\n- **b: If no onsite personnel are onsite/available, ask Parcel Pending Support/ASR Support Team member with whom you are working for direction on where keys should be left.**\n- **If you are requested to do anything out side of the scope of work, including returning to site, or dealing with a DOA, you must call/text Rodrigo.** (Phone number in Confidential Information)\n- **Tech must provide photos of any equipment that is worked on.**\n- **Tech must fill out the ServiceCallChecklist rev1\\_1.pdf COMPLETELY and have it signed by the property manager**\n- **Tech must note arrival and departure times on sign off sheet, document any site delays and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes.**\n- **During completion, tech must provide any photos, closing notes, open issues, service call checklist, sign off sheet, and name of person that released tech from site.**\n\n**RETURNING EQUIPMENT**\n\n**If any equipment needs to be returned to Parcel Pending after completion please take a photo of equipment or parts before leaving site (damaged or undamaged) to ensure responsibility. A return label will be in the shipping pouch behind the original shipping label.**\n\n**If a return label was not provided, please contact Parcel Pending immediately to obtain BEFORE leaving site, they will email a return label to you.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*A release code will be provided to you once tracking shows that parts are on the way back to our customer\\*\\*\\***\n\n**PAYMENT**\n\n2 hours on site will be paid at a fixed rate of $85 with a potential of up to 2 additional hours paid in 15 min intervals @ $40/hr.\n\n**Some issues may take long. Any time on site, after 2 hours, will need to be approved by Parcel Pending.**\n\n**Your check in/out times on this work order must match what our customer provides.**\n\nSite abort where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00\n\nSite abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site.\n\nCancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-24T11:30","end":"2026-09-24T13:30","latestStart":"2026-09-24T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":125},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":85},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":40}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":78},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $125 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana