{"job":{"id":20013479,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"POS and KDS offline, check cabling connections","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p>Port 16 from the Front Counter Dlink to port 2 on the MS225/switch in the back office</p><p><br></p><p>Make sure to test connection from port 16 from the Front Counter Dlink along with wallpatches from the VDUs all the way to the port 2 of the ms22/switch in the back office, Tech will need to bring at least 24 meters LAN cable in case cable from the Dlink to wallpatch needs to be replaced, make sure that both port 16 on the Dlink and port 2 on the switch  has LED lights once new cable is installed you can contact USD to check if all the POS and KDS are online.</p><p><br></p><p> </p><p><em>Review the “Confidential Section” listed at the bottom of the work order for specific detailed information regarding this dispatch.</em></p><p>Do not log multiple site visits on this work order.</p><p>Each site visit will require its own work order.</p><p>If a revisit is needed, close out this work order and contact Pivital ASAP to notify that a revisit will be required.</p><p> </p><p><strong><u>Tool Requirement:</u></strong></p><ul><li>300 Feet Cat 6 (Will be reimbursed up to $0.35 per/foot)</li><li>RJ45 connectors (Will be reimbursed up to $0.50 per/connector)</li><li>RJ45 crimping tool</li><li>Wire stripper / Cable scissors</li><li>Faceplates and Cat 6 jacks</li><li>Cable/Continuity Tester</li><li>8-10 foot Ladder</li><li>Spare patch cables</li><li>Zip ties / Velcro for cable management</li><li>Standard Tool Kit - including flat and Phillips screwdrivers in various sizes and needle nose pliers</li><li>Permanent marker</li><li>Digital Camera/Phone</li><li>Label maker</li></ul><p> </p><p><strong><u>Site Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Do Not Post Any Customer Photos On Social Media</li></ul><p> </p><p><strong><u>Site Security Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Government-issued photo ID required</li><li>Names of all techs going to the site must be provided in advance</li><li>Background check is required</li><li>Check-in with site contacts representing <del>**********</del></li><li>The job requires workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment</li><li>Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire</li><li>PPE – As Required by location</li></ul>","markdown":"**Scope of Work:**\n\nPort 16 from the Front Counter Dlink to port 2 on the MS225/switch in the back office\n\nMake sure to test connection from port 16 from the Front Counter Dlink along with wallpatches from the VDUs all the way to the port 2 of the ms22/switch in the back office, Tech will need to bring at least 24 meters LAN cable in case cable from the Dlink to wallpatch needs to be replaced, make sure that both port 16 on the Dlink and port 2 on the switch has LED lights once new cable is installed you can contact USD to check if all the POS and KDS are online.\n\n*Review the “Confidential Section” listed at the bottom of the work order for specific detailed information regarding this dispatch.*\n\nDo not log multiple site visits on this work order.\n\nEach site visit will require its own work order.\n\nIf a revisit is needed, close out this work order and contact Pivital ASAP to notify that a revisit will be required.\n\n**Tool Requirement:**\n\n- 300 Feet Cat 6 (Will be reimbursed up to $0.35 per/foot)\n- RJ45 connectors (Will be reimbursed up to $0.50 per/connector)\n- RJ45 crimping tool\n- Wire stripper / Cable scissors\n- Faceplates and Cat 6 jacks\n- Cable/Continuity Tester\n- 8-10 foot Ladder\n- Spare patch cables\n- Zip ties / Velcro for cable management\n- Standard Tool Kit - including flat and Phillips screwdrivers in various sizes and needle nose pliers\n- Permanent marker\n- Digital Camera/Phone\n- Label maker\n\n**Site Requirements:**\n\n- Do Not Post Any Customer Photos On Social Media\n\n**Site Security Requirements:**\n\n- Government-issued photo ID required\n- Names of all techs going to the site must be provided in advance\n- Background check is required\n- Check-in with site contacts representing \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- The job requires workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment\n- Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire\n- PPE – As Required by location","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-24T14:00","end":"2026-09-24T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":35,"max":70},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":35,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":57},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $70 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-0