{"job":{"id":19867808,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"LITnetworking LLC","title":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ GO LIVE / MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS149645","description":{"html":"PLEASE CALL METTEL SUPPORT UPON ARRIVAL 2123595319 Ticket 11646487<br/><br/>**PIAB Rack & Stack + Go Live **                       <br/><br/>Call Logan Ryan at 2123595319  when on site<br/>Data Remote CDS-9090 -MiMo Antenna & Bracket Kit<br/>-Tech to locate equipment.<br/>-Locate customer network switch in room switch/router.<br/>-Install MetTel Board and CDS-9090.<br/>-Attach antennas and power on.<br/>-MetTel will validate configurations.<br/>-Connect laptop and run speed tests over LTE. Do not use speedtest.net<br/>-Verify dial tone and in/outbound calling on all provisioned CDS9090 RJ11 ports.<br/>-Validate e911 address on one each line.<br/>-Use multimeter to verify each existing pair has a voltage of 0 on customer side of the demark.<br/>If voltage is found, locate the short/bridge and repair.<br/>-Work with customer to contact the alarms monitoring vendor and have the Fire Panel placed into test mode.<br/>-Locate/tag Elevator, Fire and Burglar lines.<br/>-Cross-connect to Fire Panel, Burglar Panel, and test.<br/>-Contact the fire monitoring vendor to confirm that they are receiving the faults, restoral, low battery and battery restore signals.<br/>-Confirm monitoring vendor sees the correct service address.<br/><br/>Single Dispatch-Standard PIAB installation and cross connect lines with new number. <br/><br/>Site Access: LCON - Anthony Monteverde-919-844-1860 <br/><br/>PIAB Lines with new number <br/>Specialty Elevator Service FXS Port 1-(984) 375-5194<br/>Specialty Burglar Alarm Service FXS Port 2-(984) 391-3153<br/>Specialty Fire Alarm Service FXS Port 3-(984) 391-3155<br/>Specialty Fire Alarm Service FXS Port 4-(984) 391-3163<br/><br/>Please review the following requirements and protocols for your upcoming assignment with Lit Networking:<br/><br/>To ensure the successful completion of this site visit, you must arrive with the following tools and materials: - A fully charged laptop with an Ethernet port and a cellphone with a hotspot device. - Cabling tools: Multimeter wire tester, butt set, punch down tool, crimpers, and wire cutters. - Hardware: RJ11 and RJ45 connectors, biscuit jacks, and 100 feet of Cat 5e/6 cable for potential device relocation. - Standard mounting kit: Drill, level, hammer, screwdrivers, screws, and anchors. - General supplies: Adjustable or open-end wrenches, a 4–6 ft ladder, and a 100 ft extension cord.<br/><br/>Work Order and Payment Procedures All work orders must be signed by the onsite Point of Contact and must clearly list your arrival and departure times. Please upload the signed Lit Networking work order directly to Field Nation. Please be advised that any forged signatures will be reported to Field Nation and will result in non-payment. Adhering to these documentation requirements is essential to avoid any delays in your payment processing. If you encounter any issues while onsite, please leave a detailed message through the Field Nation platform.","markdown":"PLEASE CALL METTEL SUPPORT UPON ARRIVAL 2123595319 Ticket 11646487  \n  \n\\*\\*PIAB Rack & Stack + Go Live \\*\\*   \n  \nCall Logan Ryan at 2123595319 when on site  \nData Remote CDS-9090 -MiMo Antenna & Bracket Kit  \n-Tech to locate equipment.  \n-Locate customer network switch in room switch/router.  \n-Install MetTel Board and CDS-9090.  \n-Attach antennas and power on.  \n-MetTel will validate configurations.  \n-Connect laptop and run speed tests over LTE. Do not use speedtest.net  \n-Verify dial tone and in/outbound calling on all provisioned CDS9090 RJ11 ports.  \n-Validate e911 address on one each line.  \n-Use multimeter to verify each existing pair has a voltage of 0 on customer side of the demark.  \nIf voltage is found, locate the short/bridge and repair.  \n-Work with customer to contact the alarms monitoring vendor and have the Fire Panel placed into test mode.  \n-Locate/tag Elevator, Fire and Burglar lines.  \n-Cross-connect to Fire Panel, Burglar Panel, and test.  \n-Contact the fire monitoring vendor to confirm that they are receiving the faults, restoral, low battery and battery restore signals.  \n-Confirm monitoring vendor sees the correct service address.  \n  \nSingle Dispatch-Standard PIAB installation and cross connect lines with new number.   \n  \nSite Access: LCON - Anthony Monteverde-919-844-1860   \n  \nPIAB Lines with new number   \nSpecialty Elevator Service FXS Port 1-(984) 375-5194  \nSpecialty Burglar Alarm Service FXS Port 2-(984) 391-3153  \nSpecialty Fire Alarm Service FXS Port 3-(984) 391-3155  \nSpecialty Fire Alarm Service FXS Port 4-(984) 391-3163  \n  \nPlease review the following requirements and protocols for your upcoming assignment with Lit Networking:  \n  \nTo ensure the successful completion of this site visit, you must arrive with the following tools and materials: - A fully charged laptop with an Ethernet port and a cellphone with a hotspot device. - Cabling tools: Multimeter wire tester, butt set, punch down tool, crimpers, and wire cutters. - Hardware: RJ11 and RJ45 connectors, biscuit jacks, and 100 feet of Cat 5e/6 cable for potential device relocation. - Standard mounting kit: Drill, level, hammer, screwdrivers, screws, and anchors. - General supplies: Adjustable or open-end wrenches, a 4–6 ft ladder, and a 100 ft extension cord.  \n  \nWork Order and Payment Procedures All work orders must be signed by the onsite Point of Contact and must clearly list your arrival and departure times. Please upload the signed Lit Networking work order directly to Field Nation. Please be advised that any forged signatures will be reported to Field Nation and will result in non-payment. Adhering to these documentation requirements is essential to avoid any delays in your payment processing. If you encounter any issues while onsite, please leave a detailed message through the Field Nation platform.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-25T10:00","end":"2026-09-25T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":220},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":9},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $220 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790182377820}
{"job":{"id":20013852,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TeleSol IT B.V.","title":"T105119: Install Broadband service","description":{"html":"<ul><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">All travel and/or other additional costs must be preapproved by Telesol. </strong><span style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">Please report all additional expenses in a counteroffer, otherwise they will not be approved when processing the payment, thank you.</span></li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">You are required to provide your email address</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\"> so that we can provide you with the link to our reporting platform (TTR).&nbsp;</span>Engineer must complete the online Telesol Ticket Report (TTR) and the WO in Field Nation before leaving site. TTR is in online form and there is no need to print it.</li><li><strong>Engineer needs to update us on ticket progress at least once every hour.</strong> If the job is taking longer than two hours, it should be reported to us immediately.</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">The bridge will open at the top of the hour. </strong><span style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">In the 30 minutes, you should check in with LCON, get access, check the equipment and join the call at the top of the hour.</span></li><li><strong>Please do not remove or take any equipment from the site unless it’s specified in the WO or instructed to by a remote support agent</strong>. Any questions or concerns from the customer about onsite equipment should be directed back to noc@telesolgroup.com.</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(22, 39, 65);\">The Provider cannot leave the site before being released by the customer or Telesol!</strong></li><li>Please <strong>introduce yourself</strong> as working on behalf of Telesol Group for<strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 221);\"><del>***</del></strong><strong>.</strong> The equipment being installed is for&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 221);\"><del>***</del></span>.</li><li><strong>Never use long distance calls </strong>unless the client provides toll free number. We will not reimburse you for long distance calls. Please insist on Microsoft Teams meeting instead.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Work Type: Professional Install</p><p>Conference Bridge will be over Microsoft Teams. Please have the app installed for easy chat and picture sharing capabilities.</p><p>Additional task details provided in&nbsp;<em>Confidential Information</em>&nbsp;section below.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of work</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Field tech to install Broadband service</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">It is <u>absolutely mandatory</u> to bring a laptop capable of reaching 1 gig speeds.</strong></p><p><strong><u>Special access requirements (if any)</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Special tools (if any)</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">** PLEASE BRING LABEL MAKER ** Please make sure it is working with ink and labels.</span></p><p><strong>Required Tool List</strong></p><ul><li>Screwdriver and Rack Screws for racking/mounting equipment</li><li>Label Maker</li><li>Mobile Internet access with charger (hot spot)</li><li>Mobile phone with charger</li><li>Mask &amp; gloves available (PPE as needed) if customer requires</li><li>Windows based laptop with charger (no Chromebook, mac, or tablets)</li><li>Laptop with ethernet connection (via built‑in port or USB‑to‑Ethernet adapter) must support speeds up to <strong>1000 Mbps (1G)</strong>, Teamveiwer software installed</li><li>Ability to change/assign static IP on Laptop (Admin Access)</li><li>Screen sharing software (AnyDesk):</li><li>Hyper-Terminal/Putty or other console emulator software:</li><li>1G USB-Ethernet Adapter with correct drivers and ready to use</li><li>Cisco DB9 to Serial USB Adapter</li><li>Cisco RJ-45 to Serial USB Adapter</li><li>Standard DB9 to Serial USB Adapter</li><li>Cisco micro-USB to Serial USB Adapter</li><li>Spare cables to be left at the site as needed:</li><li>(4-6) Ethernet cables</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Preferred but not required</em></strong></p><ul><li>SC-LC and LC-LC Single Mode Fiber and Multi-Mode Fiber Patch Cables</li><li>Standard Telecom tool set (snips, punch down, crimpers, cable toner/probe, wire strippers, etc.) For Legacy Products DSL, Voice etc.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Escalation Process</strong></p><ul><li><strong><em>Any issues or questions should be escalated to&nbsp;noc@telesolgroup.com</em></strong></li><li><strong><em>Contact</em></strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\"><em>&nbsp;number - ​USA Toll-free:&nbsp;</em></strong><strong><em><u><del>** ***** ********</del></u></em></strong></li></ul>","markdown":"- **All travel and/or other additional costs must be preapproved by Telesol.** Please report all additional expenses in a counteroffer, otherwise they will not be approved when processing the payment, thank you.\n- **You are required to provide your email address** so that we can provide you with the link to our reporting platform (TTR). Engineer must complete the online Telesol Ticket Report (TTR) and the WO in Field Nation before leaving site. TTR is in online form and there is no need to print it.\n- **Engineer needs to update us on ticket progress at least once every hour.** If the job is taking longer than two hours, it should be reported to us immediately.\n- **The bridge will open at the top of the hour.** In the 30 minutes, you should check in with LCON, get access, check the equipment and join the call at the top of the hour.\n- **Please do not remove or take any equipment from the site unless it’s specified in the WO or instructed to by a remote support agent**. Any questions or concerns from the customer about onsite equipment should be directed back to noc@telesolgroup.com.\n- **The Provider cannot leave the site before being released by the customer or Telesol!**\n- Please **introduce yourself** as working on behalf of Telesol Group for **\\*\\*\\*****.** The equipment being installed is for \\*\\*\\*.\n- **Never use long distance calls** unless the client provides toll free number. We will not reimburse you for long distance calls. Please insist on Microsoft Teams meeting instead.\n\nWork Type: Professional Install\n\nConference Bridge will be over Microsoft Teams. Please have the app installed for easy chat and picture sharing capabilities.\n\nAdditional task details provided in *Confidential Information* section below.\n\n**Scope of work**\n\nField tech to install Broadband service\n\n**It is absolutely mandatory to bring a laptop capable of reaching 1 gig speeds.**\n\n**Special access requirements (if any)**\n\n**Special tools (if any)**\n\n\\*\\* PLEASE BRING LABEL MAKER \\*\\* Please make sure it is working with ink and labels.\n\n**Required Tool List**\n\n- Screwdriver and Rack Screws for racking/mounting equipment\n- Label Maker\n- Mobile Internet access with charger (hot spot)\n- Mobile phone with charger\n- Mask & gloves available (PPE as needed) if customer requires\n- Windows based laptop with charger (no Chromebook, mac, or tablets)\n- Laptop with ethernet connection (via built‑in port or USB‑to‑Ethernet adapter) must support speeds up to **1000 Mbps (1G)**, Teamveiwer software installed\n- Ability to change/assign static IP on Laptop (Admin Access)\n- Screen sharing software (AnyDesk):\n- Hyper-Terminal/Putty or other console emulator software:\n- 1G USB-Ethernet Adapter with correct drivers and ready to use\n- Cisco DB9 to Serial USB Adapter\n- Cisco RJ-45 to Serial USB Adapter\n- Standard DB9 to Serial USB Adapter\n- Cisco micro-USB to Serial USB Adapter\n- Spare cables to be left at the site as needed:\n- (4-6) Ethernet cables\n\n***Preferred but not required***\n\n- SC-LC and LC-LC Single Mode Fiber and Multi-Mode Fiber Patch Cables\n- Standard Telecom tool set (snips, punch down, crimpers, cable toner/probe, wire strippers, etc.) For Legacy Products DSL, Voice etc.\n\n**Escalation Process**\n\n- ***Any issues or questions should be escalated to noc@telesolgroup.com***\n- ***Contact*** ***number - ​USA Toll-free:*** ***\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\****","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-30T10:30","end":"2026-09-30T12:30"},"payRange":{"min":140,"max":280},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":140},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":70}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":65},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $280 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00: