{"job":{"id":20015638,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Gigstreem","title":"Cortland Brier Creek - Standing by till Truck Retrieves Pallet","description":{"html":"Scope of Work – Pallet Preparation &amp; Freight Pickup *Will require provider to bring shrink Wrap.<p>GiGstreem is a national Internet Service Provider delivering high-quality service to residential and commercial properties across the country.</p><p>Work Order Location:</p><p>Residential Property – Refer to confidential notes for the exact address and onsite contact information.</p><p>Scheduled Pickup: September 24, 2026</p><p>Pickup Window: 10:00 AM – 5:00 PM</p><p>Minimum Onsite: 4 hours (may extend until 5:00 PM)</p><p>CONFIRM YOU HAVE THE REQUIRED MATERIALS AND AVAILABILITY BEFORE ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER.</p>Scope of Work<p>Dispatch a technician to locate and access the RackPak storage unit, secure an existing pallet with additional shrink wrap, and remain onsite to coordinate the scheduled freight pickup.</p><p>The freight carrier has scheduled pickup between 10:00 AM and 5:00 PM. The exact arrival time is unknown. The technician must be prepared to remain onsite for a minimum of 4 hours, with the possibility of waiting until 5:00 PM.</p>Work Details<ol><li>Locate the RackPak storage unit and obtain access.</li><li>Identify the pallet designated for freight pickup.</li><li>Inspect the pallet and apply additional shrink wrap to ensure all equipment and materials are securely packaged for transportation.</li><li>Ensure the pallet is accessible and ready for the freight carrier.</li><li>Remain onsite and wait for the scheduled pickup truck to arrive.</li><li>Coordinate with the freight driver to provide access to the pallet and assist with the pickup as needed.</li><li>Confirm the pallet has been successfully retrieved by the freight carrier.</li><li>Take photos of the secured pallet before pickup and obtain pickup confirmation or a bill of lading, if provided.</li><li>Notify the GiGstreem manager once the pickup is complete.</li></ol>Required Materials<ul><li>Shrink wrap (mandatory): Technician must supply sufficient pallet stretch wrap to secure the entire pallet.</li><li>Mobile phone for communication and photo documentation.</li><li>Appropriate tools to access the RackPak, if required.</li></ul>Important Scheduling Requirements<p>The technician must be available for the entire pickup window. Although the minimum anticipated onsite commitment is 4 hours, the freight carrier may arrive at any time between 10:00 AM and 5:00 PM.</p><p>The technician must remain onsite until the pallet has been retrieved or until otherwise directed by the GiGstreem manager.</p><p>If the freight carrier has not arrived by 5:00 PM, contact the GiGstreem manager for further instructions before leaving.</p><ul><li>Do not accept this work order if you cannot accommodate the potential wait time or cannot provide the required shrink wrap.</li></ul>","markdown":"Scope of Work – Pallet Preparation & Freight Pickup \\*Will require provider to bring shrink Wrap.\n\nGiGstreem is a national Internet Service Provider delivering high-quality service to residential and commercial properties across the country.\n\nWork Order Location:\n\nResidential Property – Refer to confidential notes for the exact address and onsite contact information.\n\nScheduled Pickup: September 24, 2026\n\nPickup Window: 10:00 AM – 5:00 PM\n\nMinimum Onsite: 4 hours (may extend until 5:00 PM)\n\nCONFIRM YOU HAVE THE REQUIRED MATERIALS AND AVAILABILITY BEFORE ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER.\n\nScope of WorkDispatch a technician to locate and access the RackPak storage unit, secure an existing pallet with additional shrink wrap, and remain onsite to coordinate the scheduled freight pickup.\n\nThe freight carrier has scheduled pickup between 10:00 AM and 5:00 PM. The exact arrival time is unknown. The technician must be prepared to remain onsite for a minimum of 4 hours, with the possibility of waiting until 5:00 PM.\n\nWork Details1. Locate the RackPak storage unit and obtain access.\n2. Identify the pallet designated for freight pickup.\n3. Inspect the pallet and apply additional shrink wrap to ensure all equipment and materials are securely packaged for transportation.\n4. Ensure the pallet is accessible and ready for the freight carrier.\n5. Remain onsite and wait for the scheduled pickup truck to arrive.\n6. Coordinate with the freight driver to provide access to the pallet and assist with the pickup as needed.\n7. Confirm the pallet has been successfully retrieved by the freight carrier.\n8. Take photos of the secured pallet before pickup and obtain pickup confirmation or a bill of lading, if provided.\n9. Notify the GiGstreem manager once the pickup is complete.\n\nRequired Materials- Shrink wrap (mandatory): Technician must supply sufficient pallet stretch wrap to secure the entire pallet.\n- Mobile phone for communication and photo documentation.\n- Appropriate tools to access the RackPak, if required.\n\nImportant Scheduling RequirementsThe technician must be available for the entire pickup window. Although the minimum anticipated onsite commitment is 4 hours, the freight carrier may arrive at any time between 10:00 AM and 5:00 PM.\n\nThe technician must remain onsite until the pallet has been retrieved or until otherwise directed by the GiGstreem manager.\n\nIf the freight carrier has not arrived by 5:00 PM, contact the GiGstreem manager for further instructions before leaving.\n\n- Do not accept this work order if you cannot accommodate the potential wait time or cannot provide the required shrink wrap.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-24T10:00","end":"2026-09-24T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":250,"max":430},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":4,"amount":250},"additional":{"units":3,"amount":60}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":2},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"pa