{"job":{"id":20014183,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TDX Tech LLC","title":"RMO PC & Printer Modernization","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Expected Time On-site: 30-45 minutes visit can not exceed an hour without approval from <del>****** *******</del></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>If any delays are reported, they must be reported to the TDX helpdesk immediately to justify on-site time exceeding 45 minutes.</strong></p><p><strong>If issues arise, reach out to WU support <del>* ***** ********* </del>If the issues are not resolved after 15-20 minutes of working with support, please escalate the issues to <del>****** *******</del> at <del>***************</del></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>THE TECHNICIAN ASSIGNED TO THIS WORK ORDER MUST BE THE TECHNICIAN DISPATCHED TO SITE. NO EXCEPTIONS!</strong></p><p><strong>The technician must present a non-expired government issued photo ID upon arrival. If the technician is turned away for not having a valid ID, or the technician sent to site is not the technician assigned to this work order, they will be asked to leave site and will not be paid.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope:</u></strong></p><p>TDX Technician will follow the steps in the provided install guide to complete the modernization of the customers RMO PC &amp; Printer by removing legacy equipment and connecting a provided USB cable directly from the PC to the printer. Tech will pack old legacy equipment and leave it on site with the MOD.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;TDX Work Order Document (attached in documents section)</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;Install Guide (attached in documents section)</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;Non-expired government issued photo ID</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;Basic PC Tool Kit</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;Spare USB Cables</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Work Description:&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>• Check in with TDX help desk at 952-912-9222.</strong></p><p><strong>• Check in with the manager on duty</strong></p><p><strong>• Locate the delivered Hardware. All sites will be sent a USB cable.</strong></p><p><strong>• Follow the instructions in the install guide to complete the modernization process.</strong></p><ol><li>Completed end of day close, print the report, and take a photo of it and upload it</li><li>Remove the legacy equipment</li><li>Connect the new USB cable (USB A connector) to the PC and the other end of the new USB cable (USB B connector) to the printer.</li><li>Set up the printer on PC per the instructions in the install guide</li><li>Have the manager on duty complete a test transaction and take a photo of the test transaction</li><li>Pack legacy equipment and leave it on site with the manager on duty</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>• If any technical assistance is needed, please contact Money Order support</strong></p><p><strong>at </strong><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>* ***** ********</del></span></p><p><strong>• Take photos of installed equipment and legacy equipment packed.</strong></p><p><strong>• Take an overview photo showing PC and Printer</strong></p><p><strong>• Completed the TDX work order document with the manager's signature</strong></p><p><strong>• Call TDX helpdesk to check out 952-912-9222.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Technician is required to supply all tools and materials needed to complete the installation. If the technician does not have the skill set, tools, or materials needed, DO NOT accept the work order. If the technician arrives on site and is not prepared, they will be asked to leave site and will not be paid.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Deliverables:</strong></p><p><strong>• Photo of the outside of the store upon arrival</strong></p><p>• <strong>Photo of the end-of-day close</strong></p><p><strong>• Photos of installed equipment</strong></p><p><strong>• Photo of test transaction with correct date</strong></p><p><strong>• Box with legacy equipment</strong></p><p><strong>• These are all required to be submitted before checking out of the work order</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Signed TDX work order and deliverables are required to be uploaded before leaving the site! Any delay in uploading the deliverables will result in a penalty of 10%.</strong></p>","markdown":"**Expected Time On-site: 30-45 minutes visit can not exceed an hour without approval from \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**If any delays are reported, they must be reported to the TDX helpdesk immediately to justify on-site time exceeding 45 minutes.**\n\n**If issues arise, reach out to WU support \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* If the issues are not resolved after 15-20 minutes of working with support, please escalate the issues to \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**THE TECHNICIAN ASSIGNED TO THIS WORK ORDER MUST BE THE TECHNICIAN DISPATCHED TO SITE. NO EXCEPTIONS!**\n\n**The technician must present a non-expired government issued photo ID upon arrival. If the technician is turned away for not having a valid ID, or the technician sent to site is not the technician assigned to this work order, they will be asked to leave site and will not be paid.**\n\n**Scope:**\n\nTDX Technician will follow the steps in the provided install guide to complete the modernization of the customers RMO PC & Printer by removing legacy equipment and connecting a provided USB cable directly from the PC to the printer. Tech will pack old legacy equipment and leave it on site with the MOD.\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n• TDX Work Order Document (attached in documents section)\n\n• Install Guide (attached in documents section)\n\n• Non-expired government issued photo ID\n\n• Basic PC Tool Kit\n\n• Spare USB Cables\n\n**Work Description:**\n\n**• Check in with TDX help desk at 952-912-9222.**\n\n**• Check in with the manager on duty**\n\n**• Locate the delivered Hardware. All sites will be sent a USB cable.**\n\n**• Follow the instructions in the install guide to complete the modernization process.**\n\n1. Completed end of day close, print the report, and take a photo of it and upload it\n2. Remove the legacy equipment\n3. Connect the new USB cable (USB A connector) to the PC and the other end of the new USB cable (USB B connector) to the printer.\n4. Set up the printer on PC per the instructions in the install guide\n5. Have the manager on duty complete a test transaction and take a photo of the test transaction\n6. Pack legacy equipment and leave it on site with the manager on duty\n\n**• If any technical assistance is needed, please contact Money Order support**\n\n**at** \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**• Take photos of installed equipment and legacy equipment packed.**\n\n**• Take an overview photo showing PC and Printer**\n\n**• Completed the TDX work order document with the manager's signature**\n\n**• Call TDX helpdesk to check out 952-912-9222.**\n\n**Technician is required to supply all tools and materials needed to complete the installation. If the technician does not have the skill set, tools, or materials needed, DO NOT accept the work order. If the technician arrives on site and is not prepared, they will be asked to leave site and will not be paid.**\n\n**Deliverables:**\n\n**• Photo of the outside of the store upon arrival**\n\n• **Photo of the end-of-day close**\n\n**• Photos of installed equipment**\n\n**• Photo of test transaction with correct date**\n\n**• Box with legacy equipment**\n\n**• These are all required to be submitted before checking out of the work order**\n\n**Signed TDX work order and deliverables are required to be uploaded before leaving the site! Any delay in uploading the deliverables will result in a penalty of 10%.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-28T16:00","end":"2026-10-28T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":60},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":56},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $60 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-31T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Halloween"},{"start":"2026-11-01T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-11-02T05:00:00.000Z","summary":"Daylight Saving Time ends"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790187162967}
{"job":{"id":"8920320780","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"CSA Solutions","title":"Higi - Repair","description":"<p>URGENT - Worker must go onsite today.</p><p><br></p><p>Unit was tampered with and displayed inappropriate videos.</p><p>Tech needs to Call Jerry at higi (Higi Technical Support: 866-818-8793 Opt 1 Opt 3 Desk: 626-269-3974) and will walk the tech through what is needed. Tech will harvest the PC and send to Higi with provided return label.</p><p><br></p><p>Use this password to access the kiosk: iENNEXJFM</p><p>If swapping out a PC, you would use:&nbsp;miker0me0g0lfech0&nbsp;</p><p>If you have questions or require technical support during the service,&nbsp;call 931-284-4999 and follow the prompts to reach the&nbsp;EMSAR&nbsp;Level II Support team for assistance (Support Hours are Monday-Friday from 8:00 AM EST until 8:00 PM EST). Provide the team member with the Work Order number,&nbsp;location,&nbsp;and problem description. At the completion of the service contact the&nbsp;EMSAR&nbsp;Level II Support team so that they can remotely verify that the kiosk is online and operational.&nbsp;</p><p>**ALL NON-EMSAR&nbsp;TECHNICIANS: You must check in from the location as soon as you arrive onsite and before you begin working on the kiosk. Call 931-284-4999 and follow the prompts. If there are any questions about the service expectations, use this opportunity to ask the Level II Support&nbsp;team.**&nbsp;</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00","end":"2026-09-23T06:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":159.09090909},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":57.2},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/23/2026, 2:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T15:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026