{"job":{"id":20016287,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Hype Telecom, LLC","title":"Network Staging, Installation, Migration & Testing – Danville, VA","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Location:</strong> 260 Ringgold Industrial Parkway, Danville, VA 24540</p><p> <strong>Site Area:</strong> Main Floor – Server Room</p><p> <strong>Date:</strong> October 2, 2026</p><p> <strong>Scheduled Start:</strong> 9:00 AM EDT</p><p> <strong>Estimated Duration:</strong> 6 hours</p><p><br></p>Compensation<p><strong>$100 for the first 2 hours + $40 per additional hour.</strong></p><p>Travel expenses are not included in the standard work-order rate unless specifically approved by Hype Telecom.</p><p><br></p>Project Overview<p>Hype Telecom is seeking an Field Engineer to perform <strong>network equipment staging, installation, migration, and testing</strong> at a customer location in Danville, Virginia.</p><p>The FE will work with a remote technical team throughout the activity. A remote engineer will be available during the intervention to guide the FE through the required technical steps.</p>Scope of Work<p>The Field Engineer will be responsible for:</p><ul><li>Arriving onsite and checking in at the scheduled time.</li><li>Contacting the required support team and following remote engineer instructions.</li><li>Identifying and verifying the equipment involved in the activity.</li><li>Staging the network equipment as instructed.</li><li>Installing the required equipment in the designated server room/rack.</li><li>Assisting with the migration of network connections.</li><li>Connecting to the equipment through console when required.</li><li>Loading or assisting with loading the required software/IOS and Vanilla files.</li><li>Reconnecting and verifying network cabling as directed.</li><li>Assisting the remote engineer with configuration and testing.</li><li>Troubleshooting physical connectivity issues when required.</li><li>Verifying equipment status after migration.</li><li>Taking clear before, during, and after photographs.</li><li>Recording equipment details, serial numbers, and any required part transactions.</li><li>Completing all required OBS documentation before leaving the site.</li></ul><p>The FE <strong>must not make unapproved configuration changes or disconnect production equipment without authorization from the remote technical team.</strong></p>Software / IOS Requirements<p>The activity involves a <strong>Catalyst 9200L</strong>.</p><p>Required IOS:</p><p><strong>File:</strong> cat9k_lite_iosxe.17.15.05.SPA.bin</p><p> <strong>Size:</strong> 480.63 MB</p><p>The FE must ensure that the required IOS and Vanilla files provided for the activity are available before arriving onsite.</p>Required Experience<p>The FE should have hands-on experience with:</p><ul><li>Cisco network equipment.</li><li>Cisco Catalyst switches.</li><li>Network equipment staging and installation.</li><li>Rack-mounted network equipment.</li><li>Network migrations.</li><li>Console access and remote-assisted configuration.</li><li>Copper and fiber cabling.</li><li>Basic network connectivity testing.</li><li>Working with remote network engineers.</li></ul>Required Tools – OBS Field Engineer Toolkit<p>The FE must arrive with the necessary tools and equipment, including:</p><ul><li>Windows laptop with charger.</li><li>Reliable mobile internet/hotspot.</li><li>Microsoft Teams, Webex and/or remote-support applications as required.</li><li>PuTTY or equivalent terminal software.</li><li>USB flash drive.</li><li>RJ45-to-DB9 console cable.</li><li>FTDI USB-to-RJ45 console cable.</li><li>USB-to-serial adapter.</li><li>USB-C-to-USB cable.</li><li>Micro-USB-to-USB cable.</li><li>Mini-USB-to-USB cable.</li><li>RJ45-to-USB console cable.</li><li>Cat5e/Cat6 Ethernet patch cables.</li><li>Materials/tools to terminate Ethernet cables when required.</li><li>RJ45 connectors and crimping tool.</li><li>Ethernet cable tester.</li><li>Fiber patch cables and fiber cleaning kit.</li><li>Appropriate fiber loopbacks.</li><li>Optical Power Meter / light meter.</li><li>Standard network loopback plugs.</li><li>Phillips and flathead screwdrivers.</li><li>Pliers, wire cutters/strippers and adjustable wrench.</li><li>Standard rack installation hand tools.</li><li>Flashlight/headlamp.</li><li>Label maker.</li><li>ESD wrist strap.</li><li>Smartphone with camera and GPS capability.</li></ul>Mandatory WhatsApp Requirement<p>The FE must have <strong>WhatsApp installed and operational</strong> on their smartphone and remain reachable by Hype Telecom throughout the activity.</p>Required OBS Documentation &amp; Reporting<p>The FE must:</p><ul><li>Review the OBS work instructions before dispatch.</li><li>Provide required real-time status updates.</li><li>Record all required travel and work milestones.</li><li>Take required timestamp/GPS photographs.</li><li>Take clear before, during, and after photographs of the activity.</li><li>Document equipment models and serial numbers as required.</li><li>Complete any required part transactions.</li><li>Complete the <strong>MSVR onsite before leaving the customer location</strong>.</li><li>Enter complete and accurate closure notes.</li><li>Complete all required OBS closure documentation before departure.</li><li>Remain onsite until authorized to leave by the remote support team.</li></ul>Mandatory Time Tracking<p>The FE must accurately record:</p><ol><li>Travel Start</li><li>Arrival Onsite / Check-In</li><li>Ticket Start / Work Start</li><li>Ticket Stop / Work Stop</li><li>Leave Site</li><li>Travel Stop</li></ol>Important Payment Notice<p><strong>Failure to follow all required procedures, provide the required updates/photos, complete the MSVR onsite, and properly close all documentation before leaving the site may result in a 20% deduction from the final payment.</strong></p>","markdown":"**Location:** 260 Ringgold Industrial Parkway, Danville, VA 24540\n\n **Site Area:** Main Floor – Server Room\n\n **Date:** October 2, 2026\n\n **Scheduled Start:** 9:00 AM EDT\n\n **Estimated Duration:** 6 hours\n\nCompensation**$100 for the first 2 hours + $40 per additional hour.**\n\nTravel expenses are not included in the standard work-order rate unless specifically approved by Hype Telecom.\n\nProject OverviewHype Telecom is seeking an Field Engineer to perform **network equipment staging, installation, migration, and testing** at a customer location in Danville, Virginia.\n\nThe FE will work with a remote technical team throughout the activity. A remote engineer will be available during the intervention to guide the FE through the required technical steps.\n\nScope of WorkThe Field Engineer will be responsible for:\n\n- Arriving onsite and checking in at the scheduled time.\n- Contacting the required support team and following remote engineer instructions.\n- Identifying and verifying the equipment involved in the activity.\n- Staging the network equipment as instructed.\n- Installing the required equipment in the designated server room/rack.\n- Assisting with the migration of network connections.\n- Connecting to the equipment through console when required.\n- Loading or assisting with loading the required software/IOS and Vanilla files.\n- Reconnecting and verifying network cabling as directed.\n- Assisting the remote engineer with configuration and testing.\n- Troubleshooting physical connectivity issues when required.\n- Verifying equipment status after migration.\n- Taking clear before, during, and after photographs.\n- Recording equipment details, serial numbers, and any required part transactions.\n- Completing all required OBS documentation before leaving the site.\n\nThe FE **must not make unapproved configuration changes or disconnect production equipment without authorization from the remote technical team.**\n\nSoftware / IOS RequirementsThe activity involves a **Catalyst 9200L**.\n\nRequired IOS:\n\n**File:** cat9k\\_lite\\_iosxe.17.15.05.SPA.bin\n\n **Size:** 480.63 MB\n\nThe FE must ensure that the required IOS and Vanilla files provided for the activity are available before arriving onsite.\n\nRequired ExperienceThe FE should have hands-on experience with:\n\n- Cisco network equipment.\n- Cisco Catalyst switches.\n- Network equipment staging and installation.\n- Rack-mounted network equipment.\n- Network migrations.\n- Console access and remote-assisted configuration.\n- Copper and fiber cabling.\n- Basic network connectivity testing.\n- Working with remote network engineers.\n\nRequired Tools – OBS Field Engineer ToolkitThe FE must arrive with the necessary tools and equipment, including:\n\n- Windows laptop with charger.\n- Reliable mobile internet/hotspot.\n- Microsoft Teams, Webex and/or remote-support applications as required.\n- PuTTY or equivalent terminal software.\n- USB flash drive.\n- RJ45-to-DB9 console cable.\n- FTDI USB-to-RJ45 console cable.\n- USB-to-serial adapter.\n- USB-C-to-USB cable.\n- Micro-USB-to-USB cable.\n- Mini-USB-to-USB cable.\n- RJ45-to-USB console cable.\n- Cat5e/Cat6 Ethernet patch cables.\n- Materials/tools to terminate Ethernet cables when required.\n- RJ45 connectors and crimping tool.\n- Ethernet cable tester.\n- Fiber patch cables and fiber cleaning kit.\n- Appropriate fiber loopbacks.\n- Optical Power Meter / light meter.\n- Standard network loopback plugs.\n- Phillips and flathead screwdrivers.\n- Pliers, wire cutters/strippers and adjustable wrench.\n- Standard rack installation hand tools.\n- Flashlight/headlamp.\n- Label maker.\n- ESD wrist strap.\n- Smartphone with camera and GPS capability.\n\nMandatory WhatsApp RequirementThe FE must have **WhatsApp installed and operational** on their smartphone and remain reachable by Hype Telecom throughout the activity.\n\nRequired OBS Documentation & ReportingThe FE must:\n\n- Review the OBS work instructions before dispatch.\n- Provide required real-time status updates.\n- Record all required travel and work milestones.\n- Take required timestamp/GPS photographs.\n- Take clear before, during, and after photographs of the activity.\n- Document equipment models and serial numbers as required.\n- Complete any required part transactions.\n- Complete the **MSVR onsite before leaving the customer location**.\n- Enter complete and accurate closure notes.\n- Complete all required OBS closure documentation before departure.\n- Remain onsite until authorized to leave by the remote support team.\n\nMandatory Time TrackingThe FE must accurately record:\n\n1. Travel Start\n2. Arrival Onsite / Check-In\n3. Ticket Start / Work Start\n4. Ticket Stop / Work Stop\n5. Leave Site\n6. Travel Stop\n\nImportant Payment Notice**Failure to follow all required procedures, provide the required updates/photos, complete the MSVR onsite, and properly close all documentation before leaving the site may result in a 20% deduction from the final payment.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-02T08:45","end":"2026-10-02T10:45"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":260},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":100},"additional":{"units":4,"amount":40}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":60},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $260 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790188241530}
