{"job":{"id":20015953,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TDX Tech LLC","title":"RMO PC & Printer Modernization / Printer Firmware Update","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Expected Time On-site: 30-45 minutes visit can not exceed an hour without approval from </strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****** *******</del></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>If any delays are reported, they must be reported to the TDX helpdesk immediately to justify on-site time exceeding 45 minutes.</strong></p><p><strong>If issues arise, reach out to<del> ** ******* </del></strong><del>**************</del> <strong>If the issues are not resolved after 15-20 minutes of working with support, please escalate the issues to </strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****** *******</del></strong><strong> at </strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***************</del></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>THE TECHNICIAN ASSIGNED TO THIS WORK ORDER MUST BE THE TECHNICIAN DISPATCHED TO SITE. NO EXCEPTIONS!</strong></p><p><strong>The technician must present a non-expired government issued photo ID upon arrival. If the technician is turned away for not having a valid ID, or the technician sent to site is not the technician assigned to this work order, they will be asked to leave site and will not be paid.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope:</u></strong></p><p>TDX Technician will follow the steps in the provided install guide to complete the modernization of the customers RMO PC &amp; Printer by removing legacy equipment and connecting a provided USB cable directly from the PC to the printer. Tech will pack old legacy equipment and leave it on site with the MOD. Tech will replace the printer.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;TDX Work Order Document (attached in documents section)</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;Install Guide (attached in documents section)</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;Non-expired government issued photo ID</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;Basic PC Tool Kit</p><p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;Spare Patch Cables</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Work Description:&nbsp;</strong></p><p>•&nbsp;Check in with TDX help desk at 952-912-9222.</p><p>•&nbsp;Check in with the manager on duty</p><p>•&nbsp;Locate the delivered Hardware. All sites will be sent a USB cable, some sites will also have a replacement printer. This will be confirmed during check in.</p><p>•&nbsp;<strong>Follow the instructions in the install guide to complete the modernization process.</strong></p><ol><li>Load parameters</li><li>Update firmware</li><li>Completed end of day close and print the report</li><li>Remove the legacy equipment</li><li>Install new equipment (if required)</li><li>Connect the new USB cable (USB A connector) to the PC and the other end of the new USB cable (USB B connector) to the printer.</li><li>Setup printer on PC per instructions in the install guide</li><li>Have the manager on duty complete a test transaction</li><li>Pack legacy equipment and leave it on site with manager on duty</li></ol><p>•&nbsp;Take photos of installed equipment and legacy equipment packed.</p><p>•&nbsp;Take overview photo showing PC and Printer</p><p>•&nbsp;Completed the TDX work order document with manager signature</p><p>• Call TDX helpdesk to check out 952-912-9222.</p><p><br></p><p>Technician is required to supply all tools and materials needed to complete the installation. If the technician does not have the skill set, tools, or materials needed, DO NOT accept the work order. If the technician arrives on site and is not prepared, they will be asked to leave site and will not be paid.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Deliverables:</strong></p><p><strong>• Photo of the outside of the store upon arrival</strong></p><p>• <strong>Photo of the end-of-day close</strong></p><p><strong>• Photos of installed equipment</strong></p><p><strong>• Photo of test transaction with correct date</strong></p><p><strong>• Box with legacy equipment</strong></p><p><strong>• These are all required to be submitted before checking out of the work order</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>﻿Signed TDX work order and deliverables are required to be uploaded before leaving the site! Any delay in uploading the deliverables will result in a penalty of 10%.</strong></p><br><br><p>Support&nbsp;1-888-810-8121</p>","markdown":"**Expected Time On-site: 30-45 minutes visit can not exceed an hour without approval from** **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**If any delays are reported, they must be reported to the TDX helpdesk immediately to justify on-site time exceeding 45 minutes.**\n\n**If issues arise, reach out to \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* **If the issues are not resolved after 15-20 minutes of working with support, please escalate the issues to** **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** **at** **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**THE TECHNICIAN ASSIGNED TO THIS WORK ORDER MUST BE THE TECHNICIAN DISPATCHED TO SITE. NO EXCEPTIONS!**\n\n**The technician must present a non-expired government issued photo ID upon arrival. If the technician is turned away for not having a valid ID, or the technician sent to site is not the technician assigned to this work order, they will be asked to leave site and will not be paid.**\n\n**Scope:**\n\nTDX Technician will follow the steps in the provided install guide to complete the modernization of the customers RMO PC & Printer by removing legacy equipment and connecting a provided USB cable directly from the PC to the printer. Tech will pack old legacy equipment and leave it on site with the MOD. Tech will replace the printer.\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n• TDX Work Order Document (attached in documents section)\n\n• Install Guide (attached in documents section)\n\n• Non-expired government issued photo ID\n\n• Basic PC Tool Kit\n\n• Spare Patch Cables\n\n**Work Description:**\n\n• Check in with TDX help desk at 952-912-9222.\n\n• Check in with the manager on duty\n\n• Locate the delivered Hardware. All sites will be sent a USB cable, some sites will also have a replacement printer. This will be confirmed during check in.\n\n• **Follow the instructions in the install guide to complete the modernization process.**\n\n1. Load parameters\n2. Update firmware\n3. Completed end of day close and print the report\n4. Remove the legacy equipment\n5. Install new equipment (if required)\n6. Connect the new USB cable (USB A connector) to the PC and the other end of the new USB cable (USB B connector) to the printer.\n7. Setup printer on PC per instructions in the install guide\n8. Have the manager on duty complete a test transaction\n9. Pack legacy equipment and leave it on site with manager on duty\n\n• Take photos of installed equipment and legacy equipment packed.\n\n• Take overview photo showing PC and Printer\n\n• Completed the TDX work order document with manager signature\n\n• Call TDX helpdesk to check out 952-912-9222.\n\nTechnician is required to supply all tools and materials needed to complete the installation. If the technician does not have the skill set, tools, or materials needed, DO NOT accept the work order. If the technician arrives on site and is not prepared, they will be asked to leave site and will not be paid.\n\n**Deliverables:**\n\n**• Photo of the outside of the store upon arrival**\n\n• **Photo of the end-of-day close**\n\n**• Photos of installed equipment**\n\n**• Photo of test transaction with correct date**\n\n**• Box with legacy equipment**\n\n**• These are all required to be submitted before checking out of the work order**\n\n**﻿Signed TDX work order and deliverables are required to be uploaded before leaving the site! Any delay in uploading the deliverables will result in a penalty of 10%.**\n\n  \n  \nSupport 1-888-810-8121","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-28T17:00","end":"2026-10-28T18:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":60},"payType":"fixed","payStruc