{"job":{"id":20016618,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Zayo Group","title":"Replace Existing Switches with 24-Port Juniper & Test | Connect Existing Circuit/Modem |Remote Support | UPS Drop-Off | Est. Onsite: 1.5hrs","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>OVERVIEW:</u></strong></p><ul><li>In need of a technician to replace the existing switches with a Juniper switch, test with remote support, and drop off the decommissioned switches at a local UPS Store</li><li><strong>Estimated onsite duration:</strong> 1.5 hrs (does not include the UPS drop-off; an additional <strong>$30 expense</strong> for the drop-off is already included in the compensation).</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\"><u>IMPORTANT NOTE</u></strong><u style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">:</u><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\"> </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">The $30 expense already included in the work order compensation covers the technician's trip to a local UPS location</strong></li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">CHECKOUT MUST BE COMPLETED ONSITE BEFORE LEAVING FOR UPS TO AVOID A FIELD NATION OFFSITE CHECKOUT PENALTY </strong></li></ul><p><strong><u>Requirements/Expectation:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"color: red;\">Arrive on time, as this is a hard start, and be sure to call into the bridge at the scheduled start time</strong></li><li>Any gas/travel charges must be submitted as a counteroffer for review before assignment; requests submitted after the work order is assigned may be denied</li><li><strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;have the tools required listed in the “Service Description” section in the event they are needed. Note that materials used that remain onsite (e.g. cabling) can be reimbursed as an expense</li><li>Exhibit professional behavior at all times (escalate to the Field Nation project manager listed in the work order with any issues)</li></ul><p><strong><u>Dress code:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Business casual Close-toed shoes, pants no holes, no short tanks, no sleeveless shirts</li></ul><p><strong><u>Tools Required:</u> </strong></p><ul><li>Packing Tape</li><li><u>﻿</u>Laptop with charger, equipped with Ethernet and internet connectivity</li><li>Working console cable (DB9 or USB-to-Serial with installed drivers; test before arrival)</li><li>Smartphone Fully Charged w/ Charger &amp; Camera</li><li>Mobile Hotspot (Can be your Smartphone)</li><li>Label maker&nbsp;</li><li>6’-8’ A-Frame Ladder</li><li>Ethernet Patch Cables: Quantity 3-5 (3’-10’ cat5e/cat6)</li><li>Basic Hand Tools such as screwdrivers, wrenches, pliers, cutters, etc.</li><li>Tools for either rack mounting or wall mounting equipment</li><li>Ethernet Network Cable Toner &amp; Tester</li><li>100ft Cat5e/Cat6 Ethernet cabling&nbsp;</li><li>Drill w/ charged batteries w/ various drill bits&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong><u>Pre-Site requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Review the work order information prior to the scheduled dispatch</li></ul><p><strong><u>On-Site Tasks:</u></strong></p><ol><li><strong style=\"color: black;\">IMPORTANT</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">:&nbsp;</span><strong>You are required to reference the ‘</strong><strong style=\"color: red;\">Confidential Information</strong><strong>’ section&nbsp;<em><u>IF</u></em>&nbsp;any additional details regarding this dispatch are posted</strong></li><li>Check in with the the manager on duty/local contact (MOD/LCON)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">See customer field '<span style=\"color: rgb(16, 29, 113);\">Site Contact Name &amp; Number' for MOD/LCON information (may just list&nbsp;</span>MOD/LCON<span style=\"color: rgb(16, 29, 113);\">&nbsp;and not a specific person)</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Note that the MOD/LCON may not familiar with the SOW. Please just check in with the manager on duty</li><li>At the scheduled install time, call <strong><del>************</del></strong> to check in and work directly with the <del>****</del> team</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Important</strong>: You must work with the <del>****</del> team throughout the installation process, including troubleshooting any networking equipment as needed</li><li>Take a photo of the existing network setup before starting the scope of work</li><li>Confirm the contents in the box with the&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****</del></span>&nbsp;team and notate anything that is missing in the \"Close Out Notes\" field</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Should contain a Juniper switch and a return shipping label</li><li>Working closely with the remote support team, perform the following tasks <strong>(see the attached network diagram for reference):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Only at the direction of the remote support team</u></strong>, remove the existing TP-Link or Netgear switches, confirming the make/model before disconnecting</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Install the new Juniper switch and make all connections as directed by the remote support team; verify cables are labeled and notify the team of any that are not</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Ports 0-3 = Workstation</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Ports 4-5 = Printer</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Ports 6-7 = Phones</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Port 8 = Access Point</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Port 9 = Gate</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Port 10 = Future Use</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Port 11 = Kiosk</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Port 12-21 = IoT (NVR, Camera, Thermostat, etc)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Port 22 = WattBox Network Port</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Port 23 = VeloCloud GE3</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Locate the Customer Broadband Modem</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Identify the modem’s <strong>Ethernet/network port</strong> providing the broadband connection</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Using a patch cable, connect the modem to <strong>GE1 on the Edge device</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Confirm the connection is secure and verify the expected <strong>link/activity indicators</strong> on both devices</li><li>Wait for <del>****</del> verification that VeloCloud, Juniper Switch, Cradlepoint, Wattbox are online and communicating</li><li>Using the box the new Juniper switch arrived in, securely pack the decommissioned switches for return</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Take a photo of the packed equipment before closing the box</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Close and securely tape the box</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Attach the prepaid return label included with the shipment; <strong>ENSURE IT COVERS THE OLD SHIPPING LABEL</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Take a photo of the sealed box showing the return label</li><li>Drop off the package at a local UPS location</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Upload the UPS drop-off receipt</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>Required On-Site Deliverables:</u></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Take a photo showing the completed Juniper switch and network installation</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Upload all required and any additional photos to the work order</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Email the photos to the <del>****</del> team at <del>*****************</del> Note that the team may request additional photos during the installation to assist with the installation</li></ol><p><strong><u>Escalations:</u></strong></p><p>For any questions regarding the SOW, arrival delays, or onsite concerns, please reach out to the appropriate Field Nation work order manager during the hours listed below:</p><p><strong>Contact Hours:</strong></p><p><strong><u>8:00 AM &ndash; 5:00 PM Eastern</u></strong></p><ul><li><del>***** ************</del></li><li><del>****** ************</del></li></ul><p><strong><u>2:00 PM &ndash; 11:00 PM Eastern</u></strong></p><ul><li><del>******** ******************</del></li></ul>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW:**\n\n- In need of a technician to replace the existing switches with a Juniper switch, test with remote support, and drop off the decommissioned switches at a local UPS Store\n- **Estimated onsite duration:** 1.5 hrs (does not include the UPS drop-off; an additional **$30 expense** for the drop-off is already included in the compensation).\n- **IMPORTANT NOTE**: **The $30 expense already included in the work order compensation covers the technician's trip to a local UPS location**\n- **CHECKOUT MUST BE COMPLETED ONSITE BEFORE LEAVING FOR UPS TO AVOID A FIELD NATION OFFSITE CHECKOUT PENALTY**\n\n**Requirements/Expectation:**\n\n- **Arrive on time, as this is a hard start, and be sure to call into the bridge at the scheduled start time**\n- Any gas/travel charges must be submitted as a counteroffer for review before assignment; requests submitted after the work order is assigned may be denied\n- **MUST** have the tools required listed in the “Service Description” section in the event they are needed. Note that materials used that remain onsite (e.g. cabling) can be reimbursed as an expense\n- Exhibit professional behavior at all times (escalate to the Field Nation project manager listed in the work order with any issues)\n\n**Dress code:**\n\n- Business casual Close-toed shoes, pants no holes, no short tanks, no sleeveless shirts\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Packing Tape\n- ﻿Laptop with charger, equipped with Ethernet and internet connectivity\n- Working console cable (DB9 or USB-to-Serial with installed drivers; test before arrival)\n- Smartphone Fully Charged w/ Charger & Camera\n- Mobile Hotspot (Can be your Smartphone)\n- Label maker\n- 6’-8’ A-Frame Ladder\n- Ethernet Patch Cables: Quantity 3-5 (3’-10’ cat5e/cat6)\n- Basic Hand Tools such as screwdrivers, wrenches, pliers, cutters, etc.\n- Tools for either rack mounting or wall mounting equipment\n- Ethernet Network Cable Toner & Tester\n- 100ft Cat5e/Cat6 Ethernet cabling\n- Drill w/ charged batteries w/ various drill bits\n\n**Pre-Site requirements:**\n\n- Review the work order information prior to the scheduled dispatch\n\n**On-Site Tasks:**\n\n1. **IMPORTANT**: **You are required to reference the ‘****Confidential Information****’ section *IF* any additional details regarding this dispatch are posted**\n2. Check in with the the manager on duty/local contact (MOD/LCON)\n3. See customer field 'Site Contact Name & Number' for MOD/LCON information (may just list MOD/LCON and not a specific person)\n4. Note that the MOD/LCON may not familiar with the SOW. Please just check in with the manager on duty\n5. At the scheduled install time, call **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** to check in and work directly with the \\*\\*\\*\\* team\n6. **Important**: You must work with the \\*\\*\\*\\* team throughout the installation process, including troubleshooting any networking equipment as needed\n7. Take a photo of the existing network setup before starting the scope of work\n8. Confirm the contents in the box with the \\*\\*\\*\\* team and notate anything that is missing in the \"Close Out Notes\" field\n9. Should contain a Juniper switch and a return shipping label\n10. Working closely with the remote support team, perform the following tasks **(see the attached network diagram for reference):**\n11. **Only at the direction of the remote support team**, remove the existing TP-Link or Netgear switches, confirming the make/model before disconnecting\n12. Install the new Juniper switch and make all connections as directed by the remote support team; verify cables are labeled and notify the team of any that are not\n13. Ports 0-3 = Workstation\n14. Ports 4-5 = Printer\n15. Ports 6-7 = Phones\n16. Port 8 = Access Point\n17. Port 9 = Gate\n18. Port 10 = Future Use\n19. Port 11 = Kiosk\n20. Port 12-21 = IoT (NVR, Camera, Thermostat, etc)\n21. Port 22 = WattBox Network Port\n22. Port 23 = VeloCloud GE3\n23. **Locate the Customer Broadband Modem**\n24. Identify the modem’s **Ethernet/network port** providing the broadband connection\n25. Using a patch cable, connect the modem to **GE1 on the Edge device**\n26. Confirm the connection is secure and verify the expected **link/activity indicators** on both devices\n27. Wait for \\*\\*\\*\\* verification that VeloCloud, Juniper Switch, Cradlepoint, Wattbox are online and communicating\n28. Using the box the new Juniper switch arrived in, securely pack the decommissioned switches for return\n29. Take a photo of the packed equipment before closing the box\n30. Close and securely tape the box\n31. Attach the prepaid return label included with the shipment; **ENSURE IT COVERS THE OLD SHIPPING LABEL**\n32. Take a photo of the sealed box showing the return label\n33. Drop off the package at a local UPS location\n34. **Upload the UPS drop-off receipt**\n35. **Required On-Site Deliverables:**\n36. Take a photo showing the completed Juniper switch and network installation\n37. Upload all required and any additional photos to the work order\n38. Email the photos to the \\*\\*\\*\\* team at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Note that the team may request additional photos during the installation to assist with the installation\n\n**Escalations:**\n\nFor any questions regarding the SOW, arrival delays, or onsite concerns, please reach out to the appropriate Field Nation work order manager during the hours listed below:\n\n**Contact Hours:**\n\n**8:00 AM – 5:00 PM Eastern**\n\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**2:00 PM – 11:00 PM Eastern**\n\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-09T12:30","end":"2026-10-09T13:30"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":120},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":60},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":60}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":45},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790191410934}
{"job":{"id":20017051,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Anatomage","title":"Anatomage Table - CMOS Battery Replacement","description":{"html":"<p>Our product, the Anatomage Table, is a virtual dissection table comprised of two 46\" monitors connected to a computer with a touchscreen overlay.</p>\n<p>We are looking for technicians near <strong>Greenville, NC</strong> who are comfortable building and troubleshooting computers. We ran some initial troubleshooting with the onsite staff and determined the battery needs to be replaced.</p>\n<p>Please note that images will be needed to taken through out the WO to ensure no issues during installation. If there are uploading concerns due to service issues, please inform your WO manager.</p>\n<p><strong>The location does&nbsp;<u>not</u>&nbsp;have a CMOS (CR2032) onsite.</strong></p>\n<p>Troubleshooting Includes:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Confirming that the PC is unable to power on or displays CMOS Date/Time reset error</li>\n<li>Referencing <strong>CMOS Replacement Guide</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Opening up Table and remove PC for access (Following CMOS Replacement Doc)</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Open PC and Remove old CMOS battery</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Discharge and&nbsp;<u>wait 15 minutes</u></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Install the replacement battery</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Take a photo of the PC prior to re-installation to be uploaded.</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Reinstalling PC into table</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Testing the PC, confirming it can power on and display</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Take a photo of the screens to show both are powering on.</strong></li>\n<li>Closing up the unit</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Take a photo of the table put together to be uploaded.</strong></li>\n<li>Power on and confirm touch is functioning and TableEDU software can open</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If touch is uncalibrated, follow<strong>NVIDIA Surround Set Up Guide</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If TableEDU is not activated, contact your WO Manager</li>\n<li>Additional Steps as needed</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Any questions about the installation feel free to message Anatomage.</p>\n<p>___</p>\n<p>Arrival Instructions:</p>\n<p>Check in at front with Photo ID.</p>\n<p><br /></p>","markdown":"Our product, the Anatomage Table, is a virtual dissection table comprised of two 46\" monitors connected to a computer with a touchscreen overlay.\n\nWe are looking for technicians near **Greenville, NC** who are comfortable building and troubleshooting computers. We ran some initial troubleshooting with the onsite staff and determined the battery needs to be replaced.\n\nPlease note that images will be needed to taken through out the WO to ensure no issues during installation. If there are uploading concerns due to service issues, please inform your WO manager.\n\n**The location does not have a CMOS (CR2032) onsite.**\n\nTroubleshooting Includes:\n\n1. Confirming that the PC is unable to power on or displays CMOS Date/Time reset error\n2. Referencing **CMOS Replacement Guide**\n3. Opening up Table and remove PC for access (Following CMOS Replacement Doc)\n4. Open PC and Remove old CMOS battery\n5. Discharge and wait 15 minutes\n6. Install the replacement battery\n7. **Take a photo of the PC prior to re-installation to be uploaded.**\n8. Reinstalling PC into table\n9. Testing the PC, confirming it can power on and display\n10. **Take a photo of the screens to show both are powering on.**\n11. Closing up the unit\n12. **Take a photo of the table put together to be uploaded.**\n13. Power on and confirm touch is functioning and TableEDU software can open\n14. If touch is uncalibrated, follow**NVIDIA Surround Set Up Guide**\n15. If TableEDU is not activated, contact your WO Manager\n16. Additional Steps as needed\n\nAny questions about the installation feel free to message Anatomage.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\n\nArrival Instructions:\n\nCheck in at front with Photo ID.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-29T11:00","end":"2026-09-29T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":150},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":100},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":78},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790192009919}
{"job":{"id":20017187,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Hemmersbach US","title":"Scheduled Visit - Raleigh, NC (10/14/26)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope:</u></strong>&nbsp;We are looking for an engineer to act as our&nbsp;<strong><u>scheduled visit engineer</u></strong>&nbsp;to support&nbsp;<strong>8 hours weekly on Wednesdays</strong> to support one of our sites. While onsite the assigned engineer will be given all the access needed to support this location and must properly complete the training document(s) we'll provide to ensure proper training, be onboarded with Hemmersbach, and the project.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Working technical knowledge of standard (Windows and iOS) operating systems and business software to allow for resolution of software application issues or full rebuild of the PC (image, applications &amp; Client data)</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Provide deskside support</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Working technical knowledge, in order to address service work orders, for PCs, laptops, and&nbsp;printers</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Customer facing soft skills</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Strong verbal and written communication skills</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ability to apply intermediate level of subject matter knowledge to solve a variety of common IT and business issues</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Works on problems/projects of moderately medium-complex scope</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Exercises independent judgment within defined practices and procedures to determine appropriate action</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Evaluates unique circumstances and makes recommendations</p>\n<ul>\n<li>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Hands and eyes support</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**Scope:** We are looking for an engineer to act as our **scheduled visit engineer** to support **8 hours weekly on Wednesdays** to support one of our sites. While onsite the assigned engineer will be given all the access needed to support this location and must properly complete the training document(s) we'll provide to ensure proper training, be onboarded with Hemmersbach, and the project.\n\n· Working technical knowledge of standard (Windows and iOS) operating systems and business software to allow for resolution of software application issues or full rebuild of the PC (image, applications & Client data)\n\n· Provide deskside support\n\n· Working technical knowledge, in order to address service work orders, for PCs, laptops, and printers\n\n· Customer facing soft skills\n\n· Strong verbal and written communication skills\n\n· Ability to apply intermediate level of subject matter knowledge to solve a variety of common IT and business issues\n\n· Works on problems/projects of moderately medium-complex scope\n\n· Exercises independent judgment within defined practices and procedures to determine appropriate action\n\n· Evaluates unique circumstances and makes recommendations\n\n- · Hands and eyes support","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-14T08:00","end":"2026-10-14T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":35,"max":280},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":35,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":8},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No in-hours counter slot available\nRequested: Wed, Oct 14, 8:00 AM\nChecked: Wed, Oct 14, Thu, Oct 15, Fri, Oct 16 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790192476050}
{"job":{"id":20017213,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"StrikeCheck","title":"Express Damage Assessment - StrikeCheck Appointment A-2722626","description":{"html":"<p>*Please make sure to read through all instructions to avoid a second visit to the property and/or non-payment*</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The following items need to be <strong><em>documented</em></strong>, <strong><em>inspected</em></strong>, <strong><em>tested</em></strong> and <strong><em>photographed, even if they are found to be non-damaged</em></strong>:</p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(32, 33, 36);\"><b><ul><li>Landscape Lighting : Brand Unknown : 4</li><li>Security Camera : Brand Unknown : 8</li><li>Router : StarLink : 1</li><li>Modem : StarLink : 1</li></ul></b></span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>ATTENTION: Every technician must use the CCG IQ Inspection Wizard to submit their findings. We cannot complete our payment to you if the findings are submitted to the Field Nation platform or via email. All findings, including non-damaged items on your list, must be sent directly to StrikeCheck using our CCG IQ Inspection Wizard via our Android app or web portal. If any item cannot be documented you must include a statement in your notes explaining those circumstances.</strong></p><p><strong>If you are unsure of how to use our Android app or web portal, or are having issues while you are onsite, please call (888) 980-8544 and a live representative will talk you through the submission process. Android users will need to download the \"CCG IQ Inspection Wizard\" in the app store on your device. Our office hours are 8am-8pm EST Monday-Friday and 8am-5pm on Saturdays. If no one is available to take your call please leave a message and we will return your call ASAP!</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Testing and Documentation Requirements:</strong></p><ol><li>Full testing and documentation procedures on a per-item type basis can be found under the “Resources” tab in our web app. Select “StrikeCheck” in the “Libraries” folder to review the requirements before every inspection to ensure all required data is being captured.</li><li>Basic continuity/ohm testing is required using a digital multimeter. Verify a functional power source or outlet with your meter and document those readings. If needed, reset any associated circuit breakers but do not otherwise alter the electrical panel.&nbsp;</li><li>Apply power and operationally test ALL FUNCTIONS of every item. Notate any connected items (speakers to receiver, cameras to DVR, etc.) and advise if further testing is necessary due to the failure of one of those components (\"Can't test speakers due to damaged receiver\").&nbsp;</li><li>Document and photograph all obtainable readings/testing. <strong>If the item is not damaged or has already been replaced with new equipment, we still need the same amount of evidence (photos and test results) to support your findings.</strong> If the item is not operating properly, determine the causation of damage.&nbsp;</li><li>In addition to photos of the loss location and your meter readings, we require that you provide a minimum of 3 pictures per item. These pictures should illustrate where/how the item is installed, the overall condition of the item, any visual damages, and <strong><em>most importantly, </em></strong>the data plate. Also photograph any associated components connected to the item you are inspecting. Additional photographs and documentation are always encouraged.</li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Inspection Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>A smart phone with access to our Android app or web app portal for Apple iOS users is the preferred method to document and upload your findings in real time. Access the app or portal before the inspection begins and it will walk you through all steps required for each item you enter.</li><li>Use of a camera and our Technician Worksheets is an alternate option that will require a computer to access the web app portal in order to upload photos as well as transcribing your detailed technical documentation from the worksheets into our system.</li><li>Multimeter/VOM and a basic toolkit</li><li>Must be professionally dressed (wear a clean collared shirt and pants; No shorts, no t-shirts, no flip-flops, and no ripped jeans). Avoid wearing anything that will identify your personal employer/company name or contact info to prevent insureds from calling you directly after you complete your assignment. This is an independent inspection on behalf of StrikeCheck, an insurance consulting company. <strong>You</strong> <strong>must represent yourself as being with StrikeCheck</strong> <strong>when you arrive onsite</strong>.</li><li>Must be willing to display contractor photo identification (if issued) and must have appropriate background and skills to perform the listed work order requirements</li><li>Must have passed a background check and drug test.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Submission Requirements:</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>iPhone/iPad users: Upload required information via our <strong>web portal</strong> the same day as the inspection using a secure password. Click the \"Login\" link below or use this web address to access the portal:&nbsp;https://consolidatedclaims.my.site.com/ccginspector/&nbsp;</li><li>All findings, pictures, and determinations should be submitted on the same day as the inspection. <strong>Your deadline to submit is 24 hours from the scheduled appointment start time. Failure to do so may result in non-payment and could affect your rating.</strong></li><li>Your work order is not considered complete and payable until findings are submitted through the Android app or web portal and is approved by our Processing Department. Please make yourself available for follow-up calls if we have any questions regarding your findings.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">Scheduling Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>These work orders most likely take place in a residential property, and therefore requires the ETA to be approved by the client.</li><li>When you are assigned this work order, please submit an ETA as soon as possible.</li><li>We will reach out to the client to confirm that they are able to be onsite during your proposed ETA. <strong><u>The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.</u></strong></li><li>A project manager will message you via the Field Nation App when the ETA has been confirmed with the insured. If you go to the loss location before we confirm the appointment is set, you will not be afforded a trip fee in the event that the insured is not present when you arrive.</li><li><strong>You must update our project managers and dispatch coordinators regularly on work order progress, any service delays, or schedule conflicts. If you cannot make an appointment CALL OUR OFFICE IMMEDIATELY TO RESCHEDULE. Field Nation messages are not an accepted medium for rescheduling or canceling appointments!</strong></li><li>If you go to the property, but the client does not show for the appointment, call us immediately so we can follow up with the client and determine if they will be arriving soon. <strong>If the client misses the appointment, you must take a clear photo of the house/property, showing the address so we can confirm you were there.</strong></li><li>StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the insured cannot make the appointment.&nbsp;</li><li>StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the scope of work cannot be completed for any reason</li><li>StrikeCheck will <em>not </em>provide a trip fee if you arrive at an appointment that has <em>not </em>been confirmed with the client and the project manager. <strong><u>The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.</u></strong></li></ul>","markdown":"\\*Please make sure to read through all instructions to avoid a second visit to the property and/or non-payment\\*\n\nThe following items need to be ***documented***, ***inspected***, ***tested*** and ***photographed, even if they are found to be non-damaged***:\n\n**- Landscape Lighting : Brand Unknown : 4\n\\- Security Camera : Brand Unknown : 8\n\\- Router : StarLink : 1\n\\- Modem : StarLink : 1**\n\n**ATTENTION: Every technician must use the CCG IQ Inspection Wizard to submit their findings. We cannot complete our payment to you if the findings are submitted to the Field Nation platform or via email. All findings, including non-damaged items on your list, must be sent directly to StrikeCheck using our CCG IQ Inspection Wizard via our Android app or web portal. If any item cannot be documented you must include a statement in your notes explaining those circumstances.**\n\n**If you are unsure of how to use our Android app or web portal, or are having issues while you are onsite, please call (888) 980-8544 and a live representative will talk you through the submission process. Android users will need to download the \"CCG IQ Inspection Wizard\" in the app store on your device. Our office hours are 8am-8pm EST Monday-Friday and 8am-5pm on Saturdays. If no one is available to take your call please leave a message and we will return your call ASAP!**\n\n**Testing and Documentation Requirements:**\n\n1. Full testing and documentation procedures on a per-item type basis can be found under the “Resources” tab in our web app. Select “StrikeCheck” in the “Libraries” folder to review the requirements before every inspection to ensure all required data is being captured.\n2. Basic continuity/ohm testing is required using a digital multimeter. Verify a functional power source or outlet with your meter and document those readings. If needed, reset any associated circuit breakers but do not otherwise alter the electrical panel.\n3. Apply power and operationally test ALL FUNCTIONS of every item. Notate any connected items (speakers to receiver, cameras to DVR, etc.) and advise if further testing is necessary due to the failure of one of those components (\"Can't test speakers due to damaged receiver\").\n4. Document and photograph all obtainable readings/testing. **If the item is not damaged or has already been replaced with new equipment, we still need the same amount of evidence (photos and test results) to support your findings.** If the item is not operating properly, determine the causation of damage.\n5. In addition to photos of the loss location and your meter readings, we require that you provide a minimum of 3 pictures per item. These pictures should illustrate where/how the item is installed, the overall condition of the item, any visual damages, and ***most importantly,*** the data plate. Also photograph any associated components connected to the item you are inspecting. Additional photographs and documentation are always encouraged.\n\n**Inspection Requirements:**\n\n- A smart phone with access to our Android app or web app portal for Apple iOS users is the preferred method to document and upload your findings in real time. Access the app or portal before the inspection begins and it will walk you through all steps required for each item you enter.\n- Use of a camera and our Technician Worksheets is an alternate option that will require a computer to access the web app portal in order to upload photos as well as transcribing your detailed technical documentation from the worksheets into our system.\n- Multimeter/VOM and a basic toolkit\n- Must be professionally dressed (wear a clean collared shirt and pants; No shorts, no t-shirts, no flip-flops, and no ripped jeans). Avoid wearing anything that will identify your personal employer/company name or contact info to prevent insureds from calling you directly after you complete your assignment. This is an independent inspection on behalf of StrikeCheck, an insurance consulting company. **You** **must represent yourself as being with StrikeCheck** **when you arrive onsite**.\n- Must be willing to display contractor photo identification (if issued) and must have appropriate background and skills to perform the listed work order requirements\n- Must have passed a background check and drug test.\n\n**Submission Requirements:**\n\n- iPhone/iPad users: Upload required information via our **web portal** the same day as the inspection using a secure password. Click the \"Login\" link below or use this web address to access the portal: <https://consolidatedclaims.my.site.com/ccginspector/&nbsp;>\n- All findings, pictures, and determinations should be submitted on the same day as the inspection. **Your deadline to submit is 24 hours from the scheduled appointment start time. Failure to do so may result in non-payment and could affect your rating.**\n- Your work order is not considered complete and payable until findings are submitted through the Android app or web portal and is approved by our Processing Department. Please make yourself available for follow-up calls if we have any questions regarding your findings.\n\n**Scheduling Requirements:**\n\n- These work orders most likely take place in a residential property, and therefore requires the ETA to be approved by the client.\n- When you are assigned this work order, please submit an ETA as soon as possible.\n- We will reach out to the client to confirm that they are able to be onsite during your proposed ETA. **The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.**\n- A project manager will message you via the Field Nation App when the ETA has been confirmed with the insured. If you go to the loss location before we confirm the appointment is set, you will not be afforded a trip fee in the event that the insured is not present when you arrive.\n- **You must update our project managers and dispatch coordinators regularly on work order progress, any service delays, or schedule conflicts. If you cannot make an appointment CALL OUR OFFICE IMMEDIATELY TO RESCHEDULE. Field Nation messages are not an accepted medium for rescheduling or canceling appointments!**\n- If you go to the property, but the client does not show for the appointment, call us immediately so we can follow up with the client and determine if they will be arriving soon. **If the client misses the appointment, you must take a clear photo of the house/property, showing the address so we can confirm you were there.**\n- StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the insured cannot make the appointment.\n- StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the scope of work cannot be completed for any reason\n- StrikeCheck will *not* provide a trip fee if you arrive at an appointment that has *not* been confirmed with the client and the project manager. **The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-24T15:00","end":"2026-09-24T17:00","latestStart":"2026-09-24T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":125,"max":125},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":40},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $125 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:0