{"job":{"id":20017381,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Allergy Partners-  Installs","description":{"html":"<p><br></p><p>WWT has been contracted to assist in the deployment of new standardized network upgrade For Allergy Partners. The overall solution includes installing new Cat 6 cabling and installing new APs in the ceiling and installing new Network Switches in the rack.</p><p>Must be able to follow heat map documents and mount APs in according area.</p><p>Working with Support desk to test and troubleshooting to make sure all the new APS are online and operational before released from site.</p><p>Will need the tools and equipment to test and do basic validation of new cable runs</p><p><u>Will be Need to use Company Cam -  There is a checklist that needs to be filled out as you do the installation collect appropriate pics and videos.   Will set you up with access This is  MUST for Competion!!</u></p><p>Will Be Expected to clean up Cabling that is existing when you swing over to new switch gear.   </p><p><br></p><p><strong>This IS a FLAT Rate JOB!! Will be on site for a possible 8 hrs. </strong></p><p><strong>Tech may be required to pick up materials at a local distribution center. </strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Technicians will be selected with the following criteria:</strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Demonstrated work experience in your FN work history (including cabling, termination, patch panel relocation)</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Field Nation score specifically timeliness, back-out ranking, and marketplace score</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ability to work with other technicians.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Distance from sites (no travel provided).</p><p><strong>Technician Expectations:</strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Attend required training.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;On the bridge at all times.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Have reliable transportation.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Have the required tools identified in the Run-Book/Deployment Guide.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Follow the directions from the bridge and</p><p><strong>A fixed rate is a fixed rate, we do not accept counter offers, and we do not allow substitutions.</strong></p>","markdown":"WWT has been contracted to assist in the deployment of new standardized network upgrade For Allergy Partners. The overall solution includes installing new Cat 6 cabling and installing new APs in the ceiling and installing new Network Switches in the rack.\n\nMust be able to follow heat map documents and mount APs in according area.\n\nWorking with Support desk to test and troubleshooting to make sure all the new APS are online and operational before released from site.\n\nWill need the tools and equipment to test and do basic validation of new cable runs\n\nWill be Need to use Company Cam - There is a checklist that needs to be filled out as you do the installation collect appropriate pics and videos. Will set you up with access This is MUST for Competion!!\n\nWill Be Expected to clean up Cabling that is existing when you swing over to new switch gear.\n\n**This IS a FLAT Rate JOB!! Will be on site for a possible 8 hrs.**\n\n**Tech may be required to pick up materials at a local distribution center.**\n\n**Technicians will be selected with the following criteria:**\n\n· Demonstrated work experience in your FN work history (including cabling, termination, patch panel relocation)\n\n· Field Nation score specifically timeliness, back-out ranking, and marketplace score\n\n· Ability to work with other technicians.\n\n· Distance from sites (no travel provided).\n\n**Technician Expectations:**\n\n· Attend required training.\n\n· On the bridge at all times.\n\n· Have reliable transportation.\n\n· Have the required tools identified in the Run-Book/Deployment Guide.\n\n· Follow the directions from the bridge and\n\n**A fixed rate is a fixed rate, we do not accept counter offers, and we do not allow substitutions.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-09T08:30","end":"2026-10-09T14:30"},"payRange":{"min":450,"max":450},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":15},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No in-hours counter slot available\nRequested: Fri, Oct 9, 8:30 AM\nChecked: Fri, Oct 9, Mon, Oct 12, Tue, Oct 13 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.0